1
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,159
You two-faced devil.
You played a game again!

2
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,559
The game is over, Bala.

3
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,839
I will be the death of all of you.

4
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,759
You can't do anything to us, Sofia.

5
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,798
Burn the carts!

6
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,199
Alps, protect the cart!

7
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:19,798
Alps! Put out the fire on the cart, come on!

8
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,559
Gonca! Fatma, Halime!

9
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,599
Protect the Alps!

10
00:03:58,600 --> 00:03:59,798
As you order, mother!

11
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:45,439
Claudius knew we were coming.

12
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,599
And he also knew the road we were taking.

13
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:53,039
But how could he know this, my Bey?

14
00:04:53,040 --> 00:05:00,799
Now that dog will build a
defense line at Mudurnu Castle.

15
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:03,359
What will we do, Osman Bey?

16
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,399
We fell into an ambush and had to turn back.

17
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,679
You know the condition of our men.

18
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,279
There are wounded ones.

19
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:14,199
We will set up a quarters in Goynuk.

20
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:18,359
Let things calm down first.
Then we will make our move.

21
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:22,679
But we will never give up on war or conquests.

22
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,039
Peace be upon you.

23
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,039
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too.

24
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,519
This is the loot we shared for Goynuk, my Bey.

25
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,439
Lands are taken with swords.

26
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:45,879
A land is conquered by the sword...

27
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:50,079
...but it can only be ruled with
justice, its nation and consent.

28
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:54,519
Now this gold will improve Goynuk.

29
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:58,239
The non-Muslims will lack nothing.

30
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:01,399
I don't want to see anyone in poverty.

31
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:08,119
For this reason, Koca Bey, this duty is yours.

32
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:12,279
You will be the commander
here. Now go and fulfill your duty.

33
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,799
As my Osman Bey orders.

34
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:19,919
Goynuk will be rebuilt with the justice of Islam.

35
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,399
God willing. God willing.

36
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,879
Boran, Turhan. -My Bey.

37
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:38,999
You..

38
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,279
You will go to Mudurnu Castle.

39
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,279
You will get inside secretly.

40
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:50,879
You'll learn how many soldiers are there
the situation of the walls, everything.

41
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:53,079
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

42
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,999
Come on, brother.

43
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:01,519
Turgut Ghazi, come.

44
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,879
Let's talk.

45
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:07,839
Let's talk, Osman. Let's talk.

46
00:07:37,159 --> 00:07:37,959
Sofia.

47
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,559
You are wounded. We must retreat.

48
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,919
Get out of my way.

49
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:55,239
Bala! I will kill you with
your daughter's dagger.

50
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,759
Halime.

51
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,119
Sister!

52
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,119
Sofia.

53
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,399
Poena..

54
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:12,519
Soldiers, we are retreating.

55
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,679
Poena..

56
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,119
My daughter...

57
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,919
My daughter, what did you do?

58
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,038
Halime.

59
00:08:20,039 --> 00:08:21,399
Halime, what did you do?!

60
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,879
My daughter!

61
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,639
They are running away. Alps, follow them!

62
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:28,239
I will take your life with my own hands, Sofia.

63
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,279
My Halime.

64
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,999
Halime, hold on, hold on
my daughter, you'll be alright.

65
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,359
You will be alright, my daughter.

66
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:39,158
No, no, my daughter, you will be alright.

67
00:08:39,159 --> 00:08:41,318
Hold on, my daughter, you will be alright.

68
00:08:41,318 --> 00:08:43,719
Alps, put the goods down.

69
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:47,359
We will take Halime to Goynuk now. Come on!

70
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:51,719
Hold on, my daughter, you will be alright.

71
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,919
How is this possible?

72
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:27,959
We expected you with a greater army, Claudius.

73
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,799
Is that so, Nikitas?

74
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:34,839
I sacrificed my men.

75
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,719
To push Osman back.

76
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:41,359
To protect Mudurnu. Do you understand?

77
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:45,679
Osman's target is here.

78
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:49,438
Today I pushed him back. But
he will come again tomorrow.

79
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,119
It is very hard to defend Mudurnu in this state.

80
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:56,839
You will defend it.

81
00:09:56,840 --> 00:10:02,399
Women, children, the
elderly, everyone will fight!

82
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:07,519
We will not give Mudurnu to him.

83
00:10:09,439 --> 00:10:14,359
I have a spy inside who informs
me of Osman's every step.

84
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:18,399
We will learn his plans and take precautions.

85
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:27,639
It was impossible for Claudius to know
which road we would take to Mudurnu.

86
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:34,599
If the enemy knows where to hit, it means
he has become friends with our friend.

87
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,679
Clearly, there is a traitor among us, Osman.

88
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:44,759
We have built a state in
the nests of many enemies.

89
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:48,519
We have defeated many of them.

90
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:54,999
But these traitors among us...
They always block our way.

91
00:10:55,680 --> 00:11:02,039
It was like this before,
it will always be like this.

92
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:05,919
The Oghuzs' sleep is deep,
and its traitor is sneaky.

93
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:09,279
But a Bey never sleeps.

94
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:11,079
He always lives with suspicion.

95
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,079
This is your burden, Osman.

96
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:18,519
Sure it is. Of course.

97
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:24,719
A wolf never forgets the
plain where he was ambushed.

98
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:29,438
I will find that snake, one way or another.

99
00:11:29,439 --> 00:11:33,719
But our target will not change.

100
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:37,799
We will make Mudurnu the land
of the Turks, one way or another.

101
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,359
Sure we will.

102
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:45,679
However, the walls of Mudurnu
Castle are high and strong.

103
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,599
Our Alps are tired.

104
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:51,479
The Turkmens who set out
from Aleppo still have not arrived.

105
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:54,719
It is clear that their
arrival will take a long time.

106
00:11:54,720 --> 00:12:01,359
We must make a move so that
we do not face defeat, my Osman.

107
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:04,399
We will. We will.

108
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:10,079
Our Allah Who opens the way of battles
for us will surely enlighten our path.

109
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,039
Surely.

110
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,479
We will be victorious.

111
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:17,519
We will be victorious. There is no other way.

112
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:21,119
We will be, with Allah's help. We will.

113
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:25,039
We will be victorious.

114
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:32,799
Halime.

115
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,919
What have you done, dear?

116
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,318
What have you done? Hold on.

117
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:40,959
She's bleeding too much. Hold on, dear.

118
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,879
You will be alright.

119
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:45,039
-It's alright.
-Hold on, sister.

120
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:48,879
-Mother.
-Yes, my dear? Yes, Halime?

121
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,438
Go on. You're good.

122
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:55,039
-Mother.
-Yes, my dear?

123
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,318
Pardon me in this world and afterworld.

124
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:02,039
No. Don't say such things. You're good.

125
00:13:02,319 --> 00:13:05,719
It's alright. Halime? Halime, open your eyes.

126
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,559
Open your eyes.

127
00:13:08,439 --> 00:13:09,719
Cerkutay!

128
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:12,959
Cerkutay, you go ahead and
let Alaaddin know! Come on!

129
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,799
The damage in Goynuk will be assessed.

130
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,919
The destroyed marketplace will be built again.

131
00:13:34,199 --> 00:13:40,079
It's easy to build a new one. But we
need to restore the merchants' trust.

132
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:45,079
Their loss will be covered
and they will be helped.

133
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:50,438
Goynuk will be the trade center
of the provinces around again.

134
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,318
Justice is important in trade.

135
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,159
Both the merchants and the state should earn.

136
00:13:56,319 --> 00:13:59,159
We should establish communities for that, huh?

137
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,239
We will.

138
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:08,879
Yigit, gather the prominent
merchants of Greek people.

139
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,719
My odalisque... Eleni Hatun.

140
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:24,359
She will be very useful for
winning the hearts of Greek people.

141
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:27,359
I have no doubts.

142
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:31,239
Yet you should be careful, Yigit.

143
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:38,078
Remember. A single Chinese princess
was enough to destroy their homeland.

144
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:41,359
Indeed.

145
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,318
Peace be upon you.

146
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,119
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too.

147
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,919
Osman Bey is waiting.

148
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:50,198
-Let's not keep Osman Bey waiting. 
-We shouldn't.

149
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,719
A riot fire will start in Goynuk.

150
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:23,519
Sofia will make the fire grow bigger.

151
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:32,318
A Turk never hits without fighting.

152
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:36,639
We will start shooting the
walls of Mudurnu tomorrow.

153
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,599
-God willing, my Bey.
-God willing, my Bey.

154
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,799
Alaaddin, tell me. Are the
battering rams and catapults ready?

155
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:48,438
Catapults are ready, my Bey.
The rams have been reinforced.

156
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:51,919
We're standing ready for the raid with your call.

157
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,279
Thank you.

158
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,399
Koca Bey, tell me.

159
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:56,879
What is the situation?

160
00:15:56,960 --> 00:16:00,159
The booties of Goynuk improved our situation.

161
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:04,159
Yet alps are exhausted, my Bey.

162
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:05,999
I'm just worried...

163
00:16:06,079 --> 00:16:13,999
I don't know what we could do if
alps can't fight during the raid tomorrow.

164
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,919
My brother is right.

165
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:21,039
Besides, they say the walls of
Mudurnu are too strong, Osman Bey.

166
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,399
Do you think we can pass?

167
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:28,438
Osman Bey, I agree with the Beys.

168
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:33,359
If we get defeated in front of the
walls, it may be devastating for us.

169
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,719
I understand your concerns.

170
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:41,078
As I turned Goynuk into a land of Turks,

171
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:44,759
...I have a good move about Mudurnu.

172
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:50,239
One way or another, we will make
a huge hole in the walls of Mudurnu.

173
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,318
God willing, my Bey.

174
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,799
-God willing.
-God willing, my Bey.

175
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:01,318
With all the alps and soldiers we have,
we will be ready in the morning prayer.

176
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,479
While the noon sun is at the top,

177
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,959
...the azan-i Muhammadi will
be recited in Mudurnu, God willing.

178
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,759
-God willing.
-God willing.

179
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:12,877
May I come, my Bey?

180
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,637
Come in, Samil.

181
00:17:21,358 --> 00:17:23,598
May your conquest be blessed, my Bey.

182
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:24,959
Thank you.

183
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,799
What's the situation of nomads?

184
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,159
I informed all of them about your move, my Bey.

185
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:31,719
Warriors whose swords rusting in the sheathes...

186
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:35,239
...have turned their faces to
the frontiers, the lands of Kayi.

187
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,399
Alright, alright.

188
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:39,799
With them, we will make these
lands a permanent homeland for us.

189
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,679
God willing, my Bey.

190
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:45,959
When I told them about your cause
in Susa, they welcomed the news.

191
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:49,319
All of them will follow you to serve Islam.

192
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,319
Alright, alright.

193
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,439
Well..

194
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:57,439
We will fight for Islam to
the last drop of our blood.

195
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,799
God willing, my Bey.

196
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,759
-God willing.
-God willing, my Bey.

197
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,599
Do I have permission, my Bey?

198
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,279
Aykurt, come in.

199
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:10,239
My Bey, Bala Hatun is coming.

200
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,319
They say the situation isn't good.

201
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,039
-What?
-What are you talking about?

202
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:22,559
My Bey!
My Shahzade!

203
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,479
Alaaddin Bey! My Shahzade!

204
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,638
Help!

205
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,519
My Shahzade!
Alaaddin Bey!

206
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:34,039
What's the matter Cerkutay?

207
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,439
What is the problem?

208
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,279
My Bey.

209
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:45,599
Some got wounded.

210
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:49,878
-Hold on, sister. Brother!
-Alaaddin!

211
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,519
-Brother!
-Alaaddin!

212
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,638
Gonca?

213
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:56,199
Alaaddin, help!

214
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:59,239
-Hold on, Halime. It's alright.
-Bala!

215
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,039
Help, son

216
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,519
-What's going on, Gonca?
-Alaaddin, help!

217
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:05,839
-Brother, help!
-Mother, what happened?

218
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:09,319
-Sister.
-Bleeding too much. We couldn't stop it.

219
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,399
-Hold her. Easy.
-Hold on.

220
00:19:11,639 --> 00:19:12,759
Bring a stretcher!

221
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,839
-Bring a stretcher now! -A stretcher!

222
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,638
-Come on!
-Who did this?

223
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,799
Bring it. Let me.

224
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:22,319
-Easy, easy.
-Carry her! Come on!

225
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,919
-Come on.
-You will be alright, sister.

226
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:28,039
-You will be alright, sister.
-Our child is dying, Osman.

227
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:30,679
She risked her life for me. I couldn't stop her.

228
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:33,679
-Who did this?
-Sofia. She ambushed the caravan.

229
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:36,519
Snake has changed her skin, huh?

230
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:51,359
Seyit, come closer.

231
00:19:52,639 --> 00:19:54,359
What is it?

232
00:19:59,639 --> 00:20:02,279
Give this to Claudius immediately.

233
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,199
He should be cautious.

234
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:14,919
Osman is going to besiege the
castle of Mudurnu tomorrow morning.

235
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,999
He has a plan.

236
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:29,799
I couldn't figure it out but strict
measures can stop his plan.

237
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,239
Go now.

238
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:41,159
What's going on, Yigit Bey?
Where are you sending Seyit Alp?

239
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:45,679
To my tribe.

240
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:52,159
My merchants and goods will
come to the marketplace of Goynuk.

241
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:57,159
It seems you are the one who will benefit
from the market thing most, Yigit Bey.

242
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,279
Yes.

243
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:04,919
Well... Fertility lies in trade.

244
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:11,199
There the market is! You
can trade too, Hasan Bey.

245
00:21:11,399 --> 00:21:12,519
No.

246
00:21:12,879 --> 00:21:17,559
I trade with weapons and find gold in the booty.

247
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:22,999
The market shall be yours and
the battlefield mine, Yigit Bey.

248
00:21:24,639 --> 00:21:26,398
Right.

249
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:31,398
Right

250
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,239
Peace be upon you.

251
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:41,919
-Peace be upon you too, my Bey.
-Peace be upon you too.

252
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:57,359
What's the matter, alps?

253
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,839
Pull yourselves together.

254
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:04,279
Heathens repelled us. We
got defeated, Turgut Ghazi.

255
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:07,719
Our swords are ashamed of
getting out of their sheathes.

256
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:11,079
What are you saying? Why would you say that?

257
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:20,919
Don't you remember the night smelling like rain?

258
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:31,159
Have you forgotten the story of
Kurshad and his forty warriors?

259
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:45,679
To stop the cruelty of China,

260
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:49,999
...they passed so-called impassable walls.

261
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:54,199
They went to the palace which was
protected by thousands of guards,

262
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:59,279
...fought a battle which a mind can't
comprehend and courage wasn't enough for.

263
00:22:59,639 --> 00:23:03,719
...and they stuck the sword of
justice into the dark flag of China!

264
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:14,719
Forty warriors and forty believer
hearts fought for their freedom.

265
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:23,279
They broke the heart of
the cruel emperor with fea

266
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,559
...and made him run away from the palace.

267
00:23:31,879 --> 00:23:35,878
Now tell me, alps.

268
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:39,739
Don't you have the power
in your veins that took

269
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:43,679
Kurshad and his forty
fighters to the Chinese palace?

270
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:46,039
We do, Turgut Ghazi!

271
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:51,239
You say you do, huh?

272
00:23:51,879 --> 00:23:54,719
Then be worthy of your ancestors.

273
00:23:55,399 --> 00:23:59,759
Courage is for us and cowardice for the enemy!

274
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:05,398
Martyrdom is for us and death for the heathens!

275
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:09,398
We shall move forward!

276
00:24:10,879 --> 00:24:16,878
And only Allah knows if we come back or not.

277
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:18,919
Okay.

278
00:24:19,879 --> 00:24:30,759
Allah tested even our Prophet Hadhrat Muhammad
Mustafa with a defeat.

279
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:37,679
You can't be victorious all the time, alps.

280
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:43,919
If you don't suffer, you
can't even call it a victory.

281
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:50,039
Remember. The heart of a
volunteer is the greatest heart.

282
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:04,679
We are soldiers whose hearts
are full with desire of fighting.

283
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:17,199
We raise our swords for only Almighty Allah...

284
00:25:18,520 --> 00:25:21,199
...and lower them for justice.

285
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:32,559
We will either win the war
or become martyrs for liberty.

286
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:38,679
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

287
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:55,359
First, we need to strengthen the walls.

288
00:25:55,360 --> 00:25:57,878
Your men are really stupid.

289
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:01,599
Soldiers!

290
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:04,279
Repair the walls!
Strengthen them! Now!

291
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:17,119
Finally.

292
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:53,599
Brother, we have to be cautious.

293
00:26:54,399 --> 00:26:56,199
Okay.

294
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:16,079
By the order of the Great Emperor...

295
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:21,999
...we are rekindling the great Byzantine fire.

296
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:29,599
You will all protect this castle like knights.

297
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:33,519
We will make Osman experience
a defeat he will never forget.

298
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:36,719
Everything is for the Great Rome!

299
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:42,398
For the Great Rome! For the Great Rome!

300
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:44,919
Get the people to their places.

301
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:47,359
Everyone will learn how to fight.

302
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:49,919
Quickly.

303
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:51,398
Come on!

304
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:55,959
Come on!

305
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:15,479
Sofia.

306
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:18,559
The snake has returned to its nest.

307
00:28:26,159 --> 00:28:30,759
Brother, first we will get out of this crowd.

308
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:35,359
Then we will wear these
dogs' soldier clothes. Come on.

309
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:37,919
Okay Boran Bey.

310
00:28:47,280 --> 00:28:51,719
Sofia, you are not saying anything.

311
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:56,239
You are wounded.

312
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,759
Are you alright?

313
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:04,719
It seems Osman defeated you.

314
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:11,319
Tell me you stopped the help going to the tribe.

315
00:29:11,320 --> 00:29:15,839
If that help reaches Osman, they
will be at the walls before night.

316
00:29:16,879 --> 00:29:20,279
I burned it all. They will not receive help.

317
00:29:20,280 --> 00:29:24,439
Then what happened to you?
Why do you look like you have lost?

318
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:27,119
Have you started to feel mercy for them?

319
00:29:30,760 --> 00:29:32,119
Never.

320
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:37,959
For victory, I killed Poena,
whom I raised with my own hands.

321
00:29:39,399 --> 00:29:42,638
I killed mercy, I killed love.

322
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:45,279
For victory.

323
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:58,519
I will no longer pity anyone.

324
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:15,779
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

325
00:30:36,639 --> 00:30:38,878
It happened because of me.

326
00:30:40,159 --> 00:30:43,759
I could not protect her. I should
have been injured, not her.

327
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:51,119
Bala, how can you say that?

328
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,839
It has nothing to do with you.

329
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:55,119
It all happened because of Sofia.

330
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:57,479
That snake will pay for what she did.

331
00:30:57,480 --> 00:31:00,039
She is testing us again with the same pain.

332
00:31:00,040 --> 00:31:03,039
I should never have trusted her.

333
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:06,279
The evil alliance united again.

334
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:07,999
Two-faced devil.

335
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:12,039
The Emperor took Claudius
and Sofia with him again.

336
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:18,799
Whoever hurts our children...

337
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,999
They will surely pay the price for this. Surely.

338
00:31:33,639 --> 00:31:34,519
My daughter.

339
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:38,679
She is waking up.

340
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:40,079
Halime.

341
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:42,479
Father.

342
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:53,279
Alaeddin, tell us something good, my son.

343
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:58,079
I will save my sister, mother.
I will treat her. Don't worry.

344
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:09,279
Fools!

345
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:11,559
Get up! Get up!

346
00:32:11,560 --> 00:32:13,599
You damned woman!

347
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:17,878
Children who can hold weapons
will fight with the soldiers.

348
00:32:17,879 --> 00:32:22,279
Women and the elderly will carry ammunition.

349
00:32:22,280 --> 00:32:26,959
These fools who cannot work and only
cry will be at the front in the battle.

350
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,999
Let them be useful before they die.

351
00:32:32,639 --> 00:32:34,479
Brother.

352
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:38,919
I have never seen people that treat
their own people with such cruelty.

353
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:41,638
Soon these dogs will die.

354
00:32:41,639 --> 00:32:43,759
Let's find a weakness first.

355
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:47,759
Let's find one, come on. Let's find it.

356
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:56,839
Brother.

357
00:32:56,879 --> 00:32:59,839
Look, look. Look.

358
00:33:04,879 --> 00:33:07,959
Come on. Come on.

359
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:16,359
Koca Bey, has order been restored in Goynuk?

360
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:18,959
What is the situation of the Greek people?

361
00:33:18,960 --> 00:33:22,919
We have rebuilt the places that
were burned and destroyed, my Bey.

362
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:29,398
We talked to the merchants, listened
to their problems, and met their needs.

363
00:33:29,399 --> 00:33:30,479
Good.

364
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:35,239
The people have suffered so much oppression
that they long for justice, my Bey.

365
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:41,479
First Goynuk, then Mudurnu...

366
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:45,638
Then the lands held by the infidels.

367
00:33:45,639 --> 00:33:48,319
All will be freed from oppression, God willing.

368
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:50,559
We will set out tomorrow..

369
00:33:50,560 --> 00:33:54,319
With Allah's permission, my Bey.

370
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:57,759
Bala.

371
00:33:57,760 --> 00:34:00,919
Bala, the main duty is yours.

372
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:02,719
Goynuk is entrusted to you.

373
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,878
As you order, my Bey.

374
00:34:04,879 --> 00:34:09,237
Justice will rule in Goynuk. The
voice of the oppressed will be heard.

375
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:10,799
Okay, okay.

376
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:15,638
Take care of the prisoners and female slaves.

377
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:20,478
The girls who want to get
married will marry our Alps.

378
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:25,158
We will bring such an order to this land that...

379
00:34:25,759 --> 00:34:29,799
We will establish a foundation to
help young Alps and sisters get married.

380
00:34:30,759 --> 00:34:35,158
This way every home
will be a pillar of the state.

381
00:34:35,159 --> 00:34:37,039
You have thought well, my Bey.

382
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:41,039
The continuation of the generation
is the survival of the state..

383
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:44,399
I will take care of this quickly, my Bey.

384
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:49,757
Starting a family and raising
generations is as important as fighting.

385
00:34:49,759 --> 00:34:54,678
If you allow me, the sisters and I
will carry this burden together, huh?

386
00:34:54,679 --> 00:34:59,079
I am not allowing you. I am entrusting it to you.

387
00:34:59,080 --> 00:35:03,239
The heart of the state beats in
the battlefield and in the houses.

388
00:35:04,640 --> 00:35:11,278
Therefore, the foundation we
will establish will be our symbol.

389
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:14,679
God willing my Bey.

390
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,278
God willing.

391
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:28,239
Osman has turned Goynuk into a headquarters.

392
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:33,399
Tomorrow, he will set out
from there and attack Mudurnu.

393
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:35,399
Let him come.

394
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:40,399
My soldiers are more angry than
ever. We will never give Mudurnu to him.

395
00:35:42,160 --> 00:35:47,039
While you destroy Osman here, I will...

396
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:51,159
...set a big fire in Goynuk.

397
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:59,278
Placing Eleni near Yigit was smart.

398
00:35:59,279 --> 00:36:02,999
She is about to complete the preparations.

399
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:06,159
She will also inform Yigit about the rebellion.

400
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:12,758
This is the farthest point of the city.

401
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:16,879
They throw the garbage here.

402
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:20,399
Only we know this secret entrance.

403
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:24,159
Tomorrow Eleni will let you in through there.

404
00:36:24,160 --> 00:36:26,519
It doesn't matter, Claudius.

405
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:33,479
Tomorrow I will light such a big
fire of rebellion in Goynuk that...

406
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:37,519
...Bala will burn to ashes.

407
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:44,639
We will set a hellish trap for
Osman here that he will never forget.

408
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:49,079
Tomorrow those dirty Turks
will be destroyed forever.

409
00:36:53,600 --> 00:36:55,439
For the great Byzantium.

410
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:58,559
For the great Byzantium.

411
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:02,119
For the great Byzantium.

412
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,879
What are these, Hatun?

413
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:12,839
Flying flames.

414
00:38:15,680 --> 00:38:17,359
Who are you?

415
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:22,599
I did not choose you just
because you are brave Yigit Bey.

416
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:24,599
You chose me?

417
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:29,758
I was placed beside you by Claudius' order.

418
00:38:29,759 --> 00:38:32,159
Claudius.

419
00:38:32,720 --> 00:38:35,919
Look, everything is ready.

420
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:41,599
Tomorrow a rebellion will start
in Goynuk to destroy the Turks.

421
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:10,719
The siege of Mudurnu...

422
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:17,439
...will cause Osman to lose Goynuk.

423
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:25,278
Spare my child's life, my Allah.

424
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:28,439
You're the One Who gives and takes lives.

425
00:39:41,040 --> 00:39:43,679
How is she doing? Better?

426
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:49,199
She's not waking up, Osman.

427
00:39:49,279 --> 00:39:50,999
Her breath is too weak.

428
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:55,679
What will I do if she doesn't
open her beautiful eyes again?

429
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:58,799
I went through this once.

430
00:39:59,520 --> 00:40:01,599
Don't make me go there again, my Allah.

431
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:03,439
Hush, Bala.

432
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:06,959
My daughter.

433
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:08,959
My daughter.

434
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:10,999
Halime.

435
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:15,399
Thinking takes away my breath.

436
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:17,199
I'm so scared.

437
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:19,359
Hush. Don't do this.

438
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:22,919
She got over many things
and will get over this too.

439
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,919
Don't worry.

440
00:40:25,400 --> 00:40:27,359
She's a stubborn one just like you.

441
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,159
She takes strength from you too.

442
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:33,798
You are here for her.

443
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,399
So she will wake up.

444
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:37,559
She used to do the same before.

445
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:41,879
She used to keep saying your
name when she got a fever.

446
00:40:44,040 --> 00:40:47,479
-You go have some rest.
-No, my Bey.

447
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:50,439
You're going to have a battle
in Mudurnu in the morning.

448
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:52,039
I will wait here. You go rest.

449
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:55,278
You will need to take care of
Goynuk and our children, anyway.

450
00:40:55,279 --> 00:40:56,719
You go have some rest.

451
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:58,719
I will rest later.

452
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:05,679
Don't worry. She will be alright.

453
00:41:05,759 --> 00:41:08,839
Come on, Bala. Come on.
-Fine.

454
00:41:38,799 --> 00:41:40,839
How will we get out?

455
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:43,278
We'll go north, brother.

456
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:45,919
The woods will restrain their sight.

457
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:48,439
We need to be quick, Turahan.

458
00:41:48,440 --> 00:41:50,479
Osman Bey is expecting intelligence.

459
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,559
Okay.

460
00:41:54,160 --> 00:41:55,798
Take this.

461
00:42:06,799 --> 00:42:08,599
Come on, man.

462
00:42:11,240 --> 00:42:13,039
Someone's coming.

463
00:42:13,279 --> 00:42:14,599
You go first.

464
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:16,199
It's my turn.

465
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:18,599
Be quick, brother.

466
00:42:18,799 --> 00:42:21,278
In the name of Allah.

467
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:27,079
What's going on here?

468
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:30,519
I'm talking to you.

469
00:43:02,240 --> 00:43:05,919
Now it's good. They got what they deserved.

470
00:43:32,200 --> 00:43:34,559
Allah Almighty speaks the truth.

471
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:43,758
The Most Merciful of the merciful.

472
00:43:44,160 --> 00:43:46,719
My Allah, The Greatest of the great.

473
00:43:47,279 --> 00:43:53,879
You are the One Who heals
everyone with Your name "Healer".

474
00:43:54,960 --> 00:43:58,559
O Creator, heal my Halime.

475
00:43:58,840 --> 00:44:01,919
Don't let our joy be spoiled, my Allah.

476
00:44:02,240 --> 00:44:07,359
Even with grief, mourning
and sorrow in our hearts,

477
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:11,039
...we will fight to spread Your
name around the whole world.

478
00:44:11,040 --> 00:44:14,999
My Allah, give me and my army strength.

479
00:44:15,320 --> 00:44:19,879
Give me a chance to ruin the games of the enemy.

480
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:22,439
You let me conquer Goynuk.

481
00:44:22,640 --> 00:44:27,159
My Allah, please let me conquer Mudurnu too.

482
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:30,758
Make us victorious, my Allah.

483
00:44:30,840 --> 00:44:32,399
Aameen, my Allah.

484
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:38,959
Aameen. Aameen, O Creator.
Aameen

485
00:45:11,279 --> 00:45:13,559
Everybody grab their weapons.

486
00:45:21,880 --> 00:45:24,239
You did everything I said, right, Eleni?

487
00:45:24,360 --> 00:45:26,559
I unlocked the door of the prisoners.

488
00:45:26,759 --> 00:45:28,999
People are gathering in the square.

489
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:31,639
They all have a grudge with Osman.

490
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:34,278
Good.

491
00:45:34,680 --> 00:45:37,999
Women and children will walk in the front.

492
00:45:38,200 --> 00:45:43,719
Our soldiers among people
will set fire to everything.

493
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:47,439
Now go and hide somewhere.

494
00:45:55,240 --> 00:45:55,919
Sofia.

495
00:46:00,240 --> 00:46:03,239
We're throwing our innocent people into the fire.

496
00:46:05,080 --> 00:46:08,798
They should be burned in the
fire so Rome will stand, Hristo.

497
00:46:08,799 --> 00:46:10,919
Don't you still get it?

498
00:46:11,360 --> 00:46:14,999
Children... How about they stay out of this?

499
00:46:24,920 --> 00:46:27,119
Move, Hristo. Move.

500
00:47:09,560 --> 00:47:13,119
Take the rest to the storehouses. Come on.

501
00:47:26,160 --> 00:47:28,039
May your work be easy.

502
00:47:30,759 --> 00:47:31,839
Allah Allah?!

503
00:47:33,840 --> 00:47:35,479
Did I hear right?

504
00:47:35,600 --> 00:47:38,639
You aren't saying bad
words to me for the first time.

505
00:47:39,840 --> 00:47:42,798
Fine. I won't speak then.

506
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:45,359
Please just talk to me.

507
00:47:48,920 --> 00:47:50,479
What did you say?

508
00:47:53,320 --> 00:47:56,919
Your sister, I said... Is she alright?

509
00:47:58,960 --> 00:48:00,319
We are waiting.

510
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:02,439
She hasn't opened her eyes yet.

511
00:48:02,640 --> 00:48:05,679
If she's strong like you, she will open her eyes.

512
00:48:05,759 --> 00:48:07,159
She'll wake up.

513
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:14,599
I came here to thank you.

514
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:18,319
You risked your life for us.

515
00:48:18,840 --> 00:48:20,639
Thank you.

516
00:48:21,240 --> 00:48:23,199
My Allah..

517
00:48:23,960 --> 00:48:27,758
So many good words for me is
too much for me in one day, Kayi...

518
00:48:29,040 --> 00:48:32,079
Fatma Hatun, is this the end of the world?

519
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:34,519
I don't know if it's the end of the world

520
00:48:34,600 --> 00:48:38,999
...but too many good words
drive you crazy, I guess.

521
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:42,239
Yes, that's it!

522
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:45,519
She calls me crazy again!

523
00:48:47,080 --> 00:48:48,239
Oghuz Bey!

524
00:48:48,240 --> 00:48:51,479
Fatma Hatun! People are rioting!
There is a chaos in the square!

525
00:48:51,480 --> 00:48:52,519
What are you saying?

526
00:48:52,520 --> 00:48:55,798
-If we don't repress the riot, Goynuk will fall.
-That won't happen!

527
00:48:55,799 --> 00:48:58,919
Some alps will stay in the
castle. We are going to the square.

528
00:48:58,920 --> 00:49:00,639
I will let my mother know.

529
00:49:00,799 --> 00:49:02,159
Sisters will be with you.

530
00:49:02,279 --> 00:49:03,919
Be careful, Fatma Hatun.

531
00:49:06,720 --> 00:49:07,839
Come on, alps!

532
00:49:07,840 --> 00:49:08,559
Come onz alps!

533
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:29,039
Turks! Turks are coming!

534
00:49:29,080 --> 00:49:30,239
Turks are coming!

535
00:49:30,320 --> 00:49:33,798
-Everybody line up!
-Come on!

536
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:42,239
-Hurry up! They are coming!
-Come on, come on!

537
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:45,959
-Gather up!
-Hurry up!

538
00:49:46,120 --> 00:49:49,879
-They are coming!
-Hurry up!

539
00:50:09,600 --> 00:50:12,079
Osman is here with all his strength.

540
00:50:12,560 --> 00:50:14,798
There is nobody in Goynuk.

541
00:50:15,360 --> 00:50:17,119
Good.

542
00:50:21,640 --> 00:50:24,519
Come closer, Osman.

543
00:50:24,640 --> 00:50:25,758
Come.

544
00:50:25,840 --> 00:50:29,758
I will give you a defeat
that you can never forget.

545
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:36,359
My walls will swallow your catapult shots.

546
00:50:36,600 --> 00:50:40,278
You will go mad. Come

547
00:50:47,720 --> 00:50:49,639
O Mudurnu!

548
00:50:50,480 --> 00:50:54,119
The history of Turks will be
made here today, God willing.

549
00:51:01,640 --> 00:51:03,239
My Bey.

550
00:51:03,759 --> 00:51:05,199
What's the situation?

551
00:51:05,279 --> 00:51:07,559
The castle is full of soldiers.

552
00:51:07,799 --> 00:51:12,119
The walls are strong rocks. But there
is a water channel in the west, my Bey.

553
00:51:13,880 --> 00:51:16,559
It's the weakest spot, my Bey.

554
00:51:16,720 --> 00:51:18,119
Listen to me carefully.

555
00:51:32,120 --> 00:51:35,039
She looks better than yesterday, huh?

556
00:51:36,200 --> 00:51:38,879
She will be better.

557
00:51:39,120 --> 00:51:40,719
She will be.

558
00:51:41,240 --> 00:51:42,959
Right, my honey?

559
00:51:43,120 --> 00:51:44,359
My Halime.

560
00:51:44,480 --> 00:51:45,919
My dear.

561
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:47,758
Open your eyes.

562
00:51:47,759 --> 00:51:50,479
Your mother is here.

563
00:51:51,360 --> 00:51:54,439
-Mother! Mother.
-Yes, dear?

564
00:51:54,720 --> 00:51:58,039
Prisoners have escaped.
People gathered and started a riot.

565
00:51:58,279 --> 00:52:00,039
There is a huge chaos.

566
00:52:01,400 --> 00:52:03,679
What are you saying?

567
00:52:07,320 --> 00:52:10,559
No. We can't let hem do that.

568
00:52:10,920 --> 00:52:12,839
You stay with your sister, dear.

569
00:52:13,120 --> 00:52:15,758
-Gonca, let's go. Come on, dear.
-Let's go.

570
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:28,278
We understood everything, my Bey.

571
00:52:28,279 --> 00:52:32,719
Even if it costs us our lives, we will
fulfill this duty with Allah's permission.

572
00:52:32,720 --> 00:52:33,959
Thank you.

573
00:52:33,960 --> 00:52:36,159
Go safely. Go now. Come on.

574
00:52:36,160 --> 00:52:38,239
-As you order, my Bey.
-Okay my Bey.

575
00:52:38,240 --> 00:52:41,999
Alkeyta, Dogan, you come with us.

576
00:52:51,200 --> 00:52:51,999
Alaeddin.

577
00:52:52,080 --> 00:52:52,879
My Bey.

578
00:52:52,880 --> 00:52:55,278
Turn the catapults to the north immediately.

579
00:52:55,720 --> 00:52:58,439
Boran and Turhan will go on duty now.

580
00:52:58,440 --> 00:53:00,839
As my Bey orders.

581
00:53:00,840 --> 00:53:02,959
The elderly of my tribe!

582
00:53:02,960 --> 00:53:04,278
My Beys!

583
00:53:04,360 --> 00:53:06,479
My brave men!

584
00:53:06,480 --> 00:53:10,359
Now the infidels are waiting
for us behind the walls!

585
00:53:10,360 --> 00:53:17,639
Today, this is the battlefield where The Righteous 
and the falsehood will stand against each other.

586
00:53:17,640 --> 00:53:23,039
Tell me. Will you fight with me here?!
-We will, Osman Bey!

587
00:53:23,731 --> 00:53:27,510
Are you ready to drink the sherbet of shahada
(metaphor for swear to die in the name of Allah)?

588
00:53:27,510 --> 00:53:29,119
We are, Osman Bey!

589
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:37,839
Allah is the Greatest!
Allah is the Greatest!

590
00:53:48,520 --> 00:53:51,879
You hear the voices of Turks, right?

591
00:53:51,880 --> 00:53:55,879
They are trying to scare us!

592
00:53:56,920 --> 00:54:02,999
But they do not know that nothing and...

593
00:54:03,000 --> 00:54:05,519
...no one can scare the soldiers of Rome!

594
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:13,959
Now, in Goynuk, the rebellion fire
of Rome is burning the place down!

595
00:54:13,960 --> 00:54:19,119
And we will fight with our honour here!

596
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:20,839
In the end..

597
00:54:21,320 --> 00:54:24,559
...we will be victorious!

598
00:54:24,560 --> 00:54:28,879
We will be victorious!

599
00:54:41,759 --> 00:54:43,639
Ya Allah..

600
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:57,439
Allah is the Greatest!

601
00:55:03,080 --> 00:55:06,399
Stand tall, strong soldiers of Rome!

602
00:55:06,400 --> 00:55:10,519
Turks' cannons cannot do anything to us!

603
00:55:10,520 --> 00:55:12,679
Keep firing, Osman!

604
00:55:12,680 --> 00:55:16,959
You can only raise the dust of
these walls with those cannons!

605
00:55:16,960 --> 00:55:18,359
Fire!

606
00:55:38,880 --> 00:55:41,239
Is this all you can do, Osman?

607
00:55:59,040 --> 00:56:01,239
My Bey.

608
00:56:01,240 --> 00:56:05,319
The catapults won't be able
to break the walls of the castle.

609
00:56:11,240 --> 00:56:15,919
Even if we strike the walls for months, it's
impossible, we won't be able to get through.

610
00:56:15,920 --> 00:56:17,679
Don't worry.

611
00:56:17,680 --> 00:56:20,999
We will make a move for sure.

612
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:23,679
Give us the good news, my Bey.

613
00:56:23,680 --> 00:56:25,679
What is your plan?

614
00:56:25,680 --> 00:56:30,079
Soon it will be revealed.

615
00:56:37,080 --> 00:56:39,919
Be quiet brothers. Come on.

616
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:04,719
Hope will spread everywhere, brothers.

617
00:57:04,720 --> 00:57:08,399
Hope for Kayis, death for the enemy.

618
00:57:14,799 --> 00:57:17,758
In the name of Allah,
O Allah, brother!

619
00:57:23,120 --> 00:57:26,399
Come on! Come on!

620
00:57:28,720 --> 00:57:32,559
Turks! -The wall of shields!

621
00:57:39,920 --> 00:57:42,758
Come on! Come on!

622
00:57:57,840 --> 00:57:59,719
Is this all you can do?

623
00:57:59,720 --> 00:58:02,919
Do you think you can break
through these walls like this?

624
00:58:02,920 --> 00:58:05,199
You foolish shepherd!

625
00:58:05,200 --> 00:58:08,039
Fire! Fire!

626
00:58:28,200 --> 00:58:31,239
What is happening there?
What is happening there?!

627
00:58:38,240 --> 00:58:40,879
They opened a breach there, Claudius.

628
00:58:43,759 --> 00:58:46,079
Thanks to Allah.

629
00:58:46,080 --> 00:58:48,639
We opened a breach in Mudurnu's walls!

630
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:49,999
Alps!

631
00:58:50,000 --> 00:58:51,439
Attack!

632
00:59:39,279 --> 00:59:41,479
You are as strong as your name, Dogan!

633
00:59:41,480 --> 00:59:44,239
Your words make me proud, Koca Bey!

634
01:00:04,000 --> 01:00:06,039
Allah is the Greatest!

635
01:00:30,799 --> 01:00:33,679
Give me the flag!

636
01:01:09,759 --> 01:01:11,719
To the breach!

637
01:01:11,720 --> 01:01:15,399
All soldiers, go to the breaches and defend!

638
01:01:36,440 --> 01:01:39,359
Claudius!

639
01:01:40,799 --> 01:01:46,559
We will either die or take our city back!

640
01:02:00,880 --> 01:02:08,399
The children of Byzantine Empire.
You are all soldiers of our Emperor!

641
01:02:09,319 --> 01:02:14,758
The dastards who killed your lord
will not show mercy to you either.

642
01:02:14,759 --> 01:02:18,879
And you know this. Their
cruelty has already begun.

643
01:02:19,560 --> 01:02:23,879
And we will not allow this.

644
01:02:26,400 --> 01:02:32,359
We will either die or take back our city.

645
01:02:45,960 --> 01:02:47,758
You stay here.

646
01:02:47,759 --> 01:02:51,639
When things get chaotic here,
you will let us into the castle.

647
01:03:07,080 --> 01:03:12,999
Alps, keep your shields with you.

648
01:03:19,319 --> 01:03:20,599
Bala.

649
01:03:21,560 --> 01:03:23,919
So you are here.

650
01:03:23,920 --> 01:03:26,359
Bala Hatun, what will we do?

651
01:03:26,360 --> 01:03:30,119
They placed the children in front
of them and armed themselves.

652
01:03:31,400 --> 01:03:35,559
No, this is not something
they can do on their own.

653
01:03:35,560 --> 01:03:36,679
Oguz.

654
01:03:36,680 --> 01:03:40,318
Bahadir, take precautions, let
the archers take their positions.

655
01:03:40,319 --> 01:03:42,879
They won't make a move until we say so.

656
01:03:42,880 --> 01:03:45,479
-As you order Bala Hatun.
-As you order Bala Hatun.

657
01:03:54,279 --> 01:03:58,599
O people, we will not harm you.

658
01:03:59,279 --> 01:04:03,318
To avoid harm to anyone go home immediately.

659
01:04:03,960 --> 01:04:06,439
Immediately!

660
01:04:22,560 --> 01:04:25,839
This is a game. That archer is not one of us.

661
01:04:25,840 --> 01:04:28,639
Oguz, go after him!

662
01:04:28,640 --> 01:04:30,639
People!

663
01:04:30,640 --> 01:04:32,278
We are not shooting the arrow!

664
01:04:32,279 --> 01:04:34,039
You are falling for their game.

665
01:04:34,040 --> 01:04:36,199
We will not harm you.

666
01:04:36,200 --> 01:04:37,919
This is my last warning.

667
01:04:37,920 --> 01:04:39,839
Go home, now!

668
01:04:41,759 --> 01:04:43,919
Alps!

669
01:04:43,920 --> 01:04:45,798
Shields! Forward!

670
01:04:47,759 --> 01:04:50,278
Protect the children, sisters.

671
01:04:52,799 --> 01:04:55,199
I will not hand over my castle to you, Osman!

672
01:04:55,200 --> 01:04:56,758
This land belongs to Rome!

673
01:05:02,040 --> 01:05:05,359
Wherever my horse's hooves step is mine.

674
01:05:55,720 --> 01:05:59,039
We will send you away from this land like dogs.

675
01:05:59,040 --> 01:06:01,679
Byzantine dogs.

676
01:06:05,560 --> 01:06:08,079
Allah is the Greatest!

677
01:06:27,960 --> 01:06:29,559
The castle has fallen, sir.

678
01:06:29,560 --> 01:06:31,359
We are retreating. To the gates!

679
01:06:46,200 --> 01:06:47,839
Take down that flag.

680
01:07:34,799 --> 01:07:40,999
Allah is the Greatest!

681
01:07:42,279 --> 01:07:47,119
Allah is the Greatest!

682
01:07:47,120 --> 01:07:51,278
Glory is yours, honor is yours.

683
01:07:51,279 --> 01:07:53,359
Fly freely, my flag!

684
01:07:54,830 --> 01:08:02,278
Allah is the Greatest!

685
01:08:05,400 --> 01:08:07,359
You are making a mistake.

686
01:08:07,360 --> 01:08:09,519
You will lose your lives for nothing.

687
01:08:09,520 --> 01:08:11,999
Stop, retreat!

688
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:14,399
Surrender and go home, people.

689
01:08:15,799 --> 01:08:18,639
We are not your enemy, what are you doing?

690
01:08:18,640 --> 01:08:20,037
Stop!

691
01:08:22,120 --> 01:08:26,078
We will not harm you.

692
01:08:26,080 --> 01:08:29,358
You took everything from me.

693
01:08:31,279 --> 01:08:35,078
I will take everything from you.

694
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:42,759
Hristo.

695
01:08:45,160 --> 01:08:47,037
Let s start.

696
01:08:49,519 --> 01:08:51,118
Bala!

697
01:08:53,040 --> 01:08:55,278
You snake!

698
01:08:55,279 --> 01:08:57,639
It was you of course!

699
01:08:57,640 --> 01:09:01,518
You used them as your shield,
but I will take your dirty life.

700
01:09:01,519 --> 01:09:03,318
Alps!

701
01:09:20,760 --> 01:09:22,679
You will suffer in pain.

702
01:09:22,680 --> 01:09:24,198
You will not be able to escape!

703
01:09:40,120 --> 01:09:43,999
Because of you, my
daughter is fighting to survive!

704
01:09:45,920 --> 01:09:46,999
Is Poena alive?

705
01:09:47,000 --> 01:09:49,118
My Halime is alive!

706
01:10:05,519 --> 01:10:07,919
-Are the wells poisoned?
-Yes, sir.

707
01:10:07,960 --> 01:10:12,319
What you think is victory will be your
disaster. You will die here, Osman!

708
01:10:12,400 --> 01:10:15,599
Release us!
-Leave us!

709
01:10:15,680 --> 01:10:18,879
-Let us go!
-Stop!

710
01:10:21,480 --> 01:10:23,999
Leave us! Leave us!

711
01:10:26,320 --> 01:10:30,239
Leave him, man! He is just a child!

712
01:10:32,480 --> 01:10:34,399
Mother, are you alright?

713
01:10:34,480 --> 01:10:36,999
Mother! Mother! Help us!

714
01:10:37,080 --> 01:10:40,518
-Mother, are you alright?
-Leave my kid!

715
01:10:41,360 --> 01:10:43,599
Leave us alone!

716
01:10:43,840 --> 01:10:45,799
Leave these innocent people alone.

717
01:10:46,800 --> 01:10:50,319
-Mother! Mother!
-You vile dogs.

718
01:10:54,200 --> 01:10:56,719
I'm going to kill you! Attack!

719
01:11:17,880 --> 01:11:22,599
Don't be afraid.

720
01:11:23,400 --> 01:11:25,959
We won't harm you.

721
01:11:26,360 --> 01:11:30,039
All of you will see the justice of Islam.

722
01:11:30,200 --> 01:11:33,239
The cruel times are over.

723
01:11:40,120 --> 01:11:47,319
You will speak your language
and perform your religion freely.

724
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:50,119
Don't be worrying.

725
01:11:50,760 --> 01:11:55,399
From now on, a new era will begin in Mudurnu.

726
01:12:51,080 --> 01:12:54,119
Hristo! We're drawing back!

727
01:12:54,240 --> 01:12:56,679
Alps, go after her!

728
01:12:59,920 --> 01:13:01,639
That's enough!

729
01:13:01,960 --> 01:13:04,518
They sacrificed you for themselves and left!

730
01:13:04,760 --> 01:13:06,639
Don't you see?

731
01:13:06,960 --> 01:13:08,359
Open your eyes!

732
01:13:08,440 --> 01:13:10,199
Bala Hatun!

733
01:13:14,320 --> 01:13:15,639
Bala Hatun.

734
01:13:15,800 --> 01:13:20,279
There is a cross around his neck.
He's a Byzantine soldier disguising as an alp.

735
01:13:28,880 --> 01:13:34,239
People of Goynuk! This is
the man who shot your sister!

736
01:13:36,519 --> 01:13:39,919
A cross around his neck
and the emperor's seal on it!

737
01:13:40,040 --> 01:13:43,879
Hoo! Hoo!

738
01:13:44,519 --> 01:13:46,119
Speak.

739
01:13:48,280 --> 01:13:52,239
It was the order of Master Sofia and Claudius.

740
01:14:05,800 --> 01:14:09,239
They put ourflag down. Go raise it again.

741
01:14:10,880 --> 01:14:14,879
We avenged you. Do you see now
what kind of game they are playing?

742
01:14:15,280 --> 01:14:17,399
Do you see how they infiltrate?

743
01:14:18,240 --> 01:14:20,799
Don't you see, people?

744
01:14:21,160 --> 01:14:23,518
They turn you against each other.

745
01:14:23,800 --> 01:14:29,479
You're throwing your neighbors, sisters
and brothers into the fire because of them.

746
01:14:30,040 --> 01:14:32,599
We aren't your enemy.

747
01:14:36,640 --> 01:14:42,679
Everybody under Osman
Bey's flag, Turks or Greeks,

748
01:14:43,000 --> 01:14:47,279
...is under our protecting as
long as they follow the rules.

749
01:14:47,519 --> 01:14:56,039
But if you riot, get deceived
and rebel once more time,

750
01:14:56,360 --> 01:15:01,599
...then neither Osman Bey nor I
can keep our swords in their sheathes.

751
01:15:02,040 --> 01:15:06,319
We came here to repair this city not to burn it.

752
01:15:07,280 --> 01:15:11,199
We came here to unite people not to divide them.

753
01:15:11,640 --> 01:15:14,159
These lands belong to all of you.

754
01:15:14,840 --> 01:15:20,039
Pay your tax, show respect and live in peace.

755
01:15:21,480 --> 01:15:24,639
Now drop your weapons.

756
01:15:28,360 --> 01:15:32,239
Then you will repair this city together.

757
01:15:32,720 --> 01:15:37,159
You opened the wounds so you have to cure them.

758
01:15:50,240 --> 01:15:54,239
My Bey, Claudius ran away
through the secret passages.

759
01:15:54,480 --> 01:15:58,159
Let him run. Time is ticking for him.

760
01:16:15,320 --> 01:16:17,879
The booty found in the treasure room, my Bey.

761
01:16:18,280 --> 01:16:21,839
This booty will give everyone strength, my Bey.

762
01:16:22,320 --> 01:16:26,119
-With strength, we will conquer many other lands!
-Yes, my Bey.

763
01:16:28,440 --> 01:16:31,639
Hand out this one for the sword right of Turks.

764
01:16:31,760 --> 01:16:33,759
-Yes, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

765
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:36,319
Come on, brothers. Take it.

766
01:16:41,200 --> 01:16:43,759
My Beys and alps.

767
01:16:43,840 --> 01:16:46,558
We won against the heathens, thanks to Allah.

768
01:16:46,680 --> 01:16:49,199
Mudurnu has become a land of Turks.

769
01:16:49,240 --> 01:16:51,999
God willing, we will
prosper this place with Islam.

770
01:16:52,000 --> 01:16:54,079
-God willing, my Bey.
-God willing, my Bey.

771
01:16:54,120 --> 01:16:57,159
-God willing.
-God willing.

772
01:17:21,080 --> 01:17:24,439
They have set out, my emperor.
And they will be here soon.

773
01:17:27,840 --> 01:17:34,159
Thinking that he got a victory,
Osman will face a greater defeat.

774
01:17:34,920 --> 01:17:39,879
Turks will vanish in Bthynia tomorrow

775
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:46,159
Halime, my sister.

776
01:17:47,680 --> 01:17:51,239
I will never get angry with you again.

777
01:17:54,600 --> 01:17:58,319
In fact, I never got angry with you.

778
01:17:59,400 --> 01:18:01,919
I got angry with myself...

779
01:18:03,400 --> 01:18:05,479
...that I couldn't recognize you.

780
01:18:08,360 --> 01:18:10,999
I recognized you with my heart...

781
01:18:11,280 --> 01:18:14,518
...and brought you to our tribe.

782
01:18:14,880 --> 01:18:18,159
But I couldn't realize that you were my sister.

783
01:18:19,360 --> 01:18:21,479
I couldn't recognize you.

784
01:18:23,480 --> 01:18:29,319
I couldn't accept that you were the enemy.

785
01:18:30,240 --> 01:18:32,799
But it wasn't your fault.

786
01:18:33,320 --> 01:18:40,919
Despite Sofia's evil plans,
you managed to remain pure.

787
01:18:47,680 --> 01:18:50,039
It was our fault.

788
01:18:50,280 --> 01:18:53,119
We failed to protect you.

789
01:18:54,519 --> 01:19:01,399
We couldn't protect you but
you sacrificed yourself to save us.

790
01:19:07,600 --> 01:19:09,119
Sister.

791
01:19:10,960 --> 01:19:15,079
Did you really forgive me?

792
01:19:16,720 --> 01:19:19,319
Thanks to Allah!

793
01:19:21,760 --> 01:19:23,079
Thanks to Allah.

794
01:19:23,280 --> 01:19:25,439
Thanks to Allah, Halime!

795
01:19:25,600 --> 01:19:27,719
You are alright, aren't you?

796
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:31,359
Thanks to Allah.

797
01:19:32,000 --> 01:19:33,839
Mother! Mother!

798
01:19:34,000 --> 01:19:36,999
Mother! Halime has waken up!

799
01:19:40,320 --> 01:19:42,279
Thanks to Allah.

800
01:19:42,519 --> 01:19:45,879
Of course! Of course, I forgave you!

801
01:19:47,600 --> 01:19:52,639
My mother always says
there is good in every trouble.

802
01:19:54,080 --> 01:19:55,879
She is right.

803
01:19:56,080 --> 01:20:00,199
Look at her!

804
01:20:02,160 --> 01:20:03,839
My dear.

805
01:20:04,640 --> 01:20:07,518
Halime! Thank Allah, you have waken up!

806
01:20:09,040 --> 01:20:13,558
Thankfully, Allah spared your life for us!

807
01:20:14,360 --> 01:20:15,919
Oh my precious!

808
01:20:16,080 --> 01:20:19,399
Are you alright? Do you have any pain?

809
01:20:19,640 --> 01:20:22,639
No, mother. I'm good.

810
01:20:23,040 --> 01:20:24,879
Very good.

811
01:20:25,240 --> 01:20:26,479
Very good.

812
01:20:28,360 --> 01:20:29,839
Mother! Mother!

813
01:20:29,920 --> 01:20:33,679
Ulgen, get animals sacrificed
and hand it out to people!

814
01:20:33,680 --> 01:20:35,079
My daughter has waken up!

815
01:20:35,320 --> 01:20:37,479
Thanks to Allah! Other great news!

816
01:20:37,480 --> 01:20:39,359
Thanks to Allah.

817
01:20:39,920 --> 01:20:41,799
What is the other news?

818
01:20:41,960 --> 01:20:43,319
Mother.

819
01:20:43,440 --> 01:20:45,959
White pigeon has brought good news.

820
01:20:46,680 --> 01:20:48,839
Mudurnu belongs to Kayi now.

821
01:20:49,200 --> 01:20:52,079
Oh really? Thanks to Allah.

822
01:20:52,200 --> 01:20:53,999
What a great day!

823
01:20:54,200 --> 01:20:56,399
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

824
01:20:56,920 --> 01:21:01,239
Father has sent us orders to go to
Mudurnu when Halime wakes up.

825
01:21:01,400 --> 01:21:06,759
Oh... Halime can't go anywhere like this.

826
01:21:07,400 --> 01:21:11,439
Well.. I can go, mother.

827
01:21:12,160 --> 01:21:14,639
You still have a wound.

828
01:21:15,400 --> 01:21:19,679
She will go, mother. We'll
go slowly by a carriage.

829
01:21:23,040 --> 01:21:24,399
Fine.

830
01:21:25,360 --> 01:21:28,199
Fine. Start the preparations then.

831
01:21:36,559 --> 01:21:40,199
My Beys, our lands are growing larger.

832
01:21:40,960 --> 01:21:44,639
Yet the number of non-Muslim
people is increasing too.

833
01:21:45,120 --> 01:21:51,079
The question isn't capturing
the land but managing the land.

834
01:21:51,280 --> 01:21:54,879
A new management should be
established in Mudurnu, my Bey.

835
01:21:55,080 --> 01:21:56,919
You're right, Koca Bey.

836
01:21:57,000 --> 01:22:02,598
We'll establish such a management that
it will be the sign of our next conquests.

837
01:22:03,280 --> 01:22:08,279
And everybody will know that Kayis
bring justice and order everywhere.

838
01:22:08,400 --> 01:22:10,639
-God willing, my Bey.
-God willing, my Bey.

839
01:22:10,680 --> 01:22:12,279
-Hasan Bey.
-My Bey.

840
01:22:12,920 --> 01:22:15,879
You proved yourself with your courage and faith.

841
01:22:15,960 --> 01:22:17,919
Thank you.

842
01:22:18,680 --> 01:22:21,159
You have the command in Mudurnu.

843
01:22:21,800 --> 01:22:24,399
Thank you, my Bey.

844
01:22:26,400 --> 01:22:29,399
Repair the holes in the city walls.

845
01:22:29,800 --> 01:22:33,159
Clean the water in the wells if it's poisoned.

846
01:22:33,680 --> 01:22:35,319
Don't worry, my Bey.

847
01:22:35,320 --> 01:22:38,279
I will carry out the duty
quickly and investigate.

848
01:22:38,280 --> 01:22:39,639
Excuse me now.

849
01:22:39,920 --> 01:22:41,319
Alright.

850
01:22:48,040 --> 01:22:49,279
Peace be upon you.

851
01:22:49,400 --> 01:22:51,039
Peace be upon you too.

852
01:22:51,240 --> 01:22:54,518
Where are you going, Turgut Ghazi?

853
01:22:54,760 --> 01:22:58,759
Well... White-bearded
elders never stop. Alaaddin.

854
01:23:01,160 --> 01:23:07,679
Our conquest has hurt the heathens very
much. They will definitely make a move.

855
01:23:08,200 --> 01:23:10,919
We'll go to the borders and check around.

856
01:23:11,240 --> 01:23:13,239
May you have a safe travel.

857
01:23:13,400 --> 01:23:15,079
Thank you, thank you.

858
01:23:15,280 --> 01:23:16,879
Thank you, my Bey.

859
01:23:17,120 --> 01:23:19,199
May Allah be pleased with you.

860
01:23:19,640 --> 01:23:23,839
Come on, Solgur Agha. Time to go.

861
01:23:26,360 --> 01:23:27,839
Let's go.

862
01:23:33,880 --> 01:23:36,279
Dying in a bed is forbidden for a Turk.

863
01:23:36,519 --> 01:23:40,919
As long as those elders live,
we will never get defeated.

864
01:23:41,120 --> 01:23:43,079
For sure.

865
01:23:45,960 --> 01:23:48,359
Put it in front of the animals.

866
01:23:49,400 --> 01:23:50,558
Give me.

867
01:24:05,800 --> 01:24:07,479
Take it.

868
01:24:10,480 --> 01:24:12,399
Water is clean, for sure.

869
01:24:12,840 --> 01:24:17,199
If the water were poisoned,
the animals would have noticed.

870
01:24:19,800 --> 01:24:23,879
People! Water is clean, for sure!

871
01:24:24,200 --> 01:24:26,239
You can drink safely.

872
01:24:26,599 --> 01:24:30,079
Come on. Come on, fill your bottles.

873
01:24:30,920 --> 01:24:31,639
Here.

874
01:24:36,160 --> 01:24:38,119
Thank you.

875
01:24:45,519 --> 01:24:47,199
May God protect you.

876
01:25:02,440 --> 01:25:05,719
Come on sisters, come on.
The table is not ready yet.

877
01:25:05,720 --> 01:25:11,759
If my Hatun was here, this
table would be talking by now.

878
01:25:11,760 --> 01:25:16,239
That's how skillful my Hatun is.

879
01:25:16,240 --> 01:25:20,119
Come on, come on sisters,
they will come soon! Please!

880
01:25:20,120 --> 01:25:22,119
Come on! Come on!

881
01:25:25,920 --> 01:25:28,119
So, Alaeddin, tell me.

882
01:25:28,120 --> 01:25:30,919
Where is your mother?
How is Halime? Is she alright?

883
01:25:30,920 --> 01:25:37,119
We sent a pigeon, my Bey. But
we still haven't received news.

884
01:25:37,120 --> 01:25:39,518
Alright. Alright.

885
01:25:49,280 --> 01:25:50,159
Bala.

886
01:25:50,200 --> 01:25:51,159
My Bey.

887
01:26:00,440 --> 01:26:03,199
Why didn't you tell us you were coming?

888
01:26:07,280 --> 01:26:09,598
Huh, my Fatma?

889
01:26:11,920 --> 01:26:13,399
My beautiful duaghter.

890
01:26:13,400 --> 01:26:17,839
My Bey...
-Bala.

891
01:26:24,640 --> 01:26:26,719
Where is Halime?

892
01:26:33,480 --> 01:26:36,999
Hatun, why are you not saying a thing?

893
01:26:38,960 --> 01:26:41,999
Nothing bad happened, right?

894
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:43,919
Is Halime awake?

895
01:26:44,559 --> 01:26:47,319
Halime... How is Halime?

896
01:26:47,320 --> 01:26:48,439
Where is Halime?

897
01:26:50,680 --> 01:26:51,239
Huh?

898
01:26:58,559 --> 01:27:01,959
You cannot get rid of me that easily!

899
01:27:01,960 --> 01:27:03,999
Halime

900
01:27:08,040 --> 01:27:09,359
Halime.

901
01:27:09,360 --> 01:27:10,839
My daughter!

902
01:27:11,200 --> 01:27:13,359
Halime. My daughter!

903
01:27:13,360 --> 01:27:14,759
Come here.

904
01:27:14,760 --> 01:27:16,439
Come, come.

905
01:27:16,440 --> 01:27:19,159
Are you feeling better?

906
01:27:20,760 --> 01:27:21,959
How are you feeling?

907
01:27:21,960 --> 01:27:24,879
Look at me. Look at me.
How are you? Are you alright?

908
01:27:25,840 --> 01:27:28,679
You are. You are alright.

909
01:27:33,280 --> 01:27:36,159
She is even making jokes.

910
01:27:36,160 --> 01:27:38,399
Praise be she is really strong.

911
01:27:39,800 --> 01:27:41,799
May your victory be blessed my Bey.

912
01:27:41,800 --> 01:27:43,558
Thank you. Thank you.

913
01:27:43,559 --> 01:27:47,479
When I have you with me... I
have my daughter with me here...

914
01:27:47,480 --> 01:27:50,679
There is no greater victory than that.

915
01:27:54,920 --> 01:27:57,639
What happened?

916
01:27:57,640 --> 01:28:00,839
It seems like you want to say something.

917
01:28:00,840 --> 01:28:06,039
I didn't want to ruin your reunion
but there was a rebellion in Goynuk.

918
01:28:07,280 --> 01:28:10,319
We suppressed it. Don't worry.

919
01:28:19,720 --> 01:28:22,279
Who did it?

920
01:28:22,280 --> 01:28:23,639
Did you catch them?

921
01:28:23,640 --> 01:28:24,919
Sofia.

922
01:28:24,920 --> 01:28:29,239
She came to finish what
she started. But she failed.

923
01:28:29,240 --> 01:28:31,199
I wounded her, she escaped.

924
01:28:31,200 --> 01:28:33,159
She won't escape again.

925
01:28:41,640 --> 01:28:45,199
Since you suppressed it, okay then.

926
01:28:45,320 --> 01:28:49,359
No one can ruin our happiness
today. My daughter is here with me too.

927
01:28:49,360 --> 01:28:53,639
Let's go then. Come on, come on, come on.

928
01:29:02,360 --> 01:29:04,518
Hatun.

929
01:29:10,800 --> 01:29:18,119
It doesn't look like your
tables but we will eat anyway.

930
01:29:18,120 --> 01:29:21,479
Can anyone compete with you?

931
01:29:21,920 --> 01:29:23,919
Sure, they cannot cook like I do.

932
01:29:23,920 --> 01:29:25,039
Right.

933
01:29:25,040 --> 01:29:27,518
But it's good, I will handle it.

934
01:29:27,519 --> 01:29:29,439
The table needs your touch.

935
01:29:30,320 --> 01:29:34,799
Father, stop talking. Let's eat.

936
01:29:34,800 --> 01:29:36,679
I have come a long way, I am hungry.

937
01:29:41,400 --> 01:29:44,839
See? See.. Did you hear him?

938
01:29:44,840 --> 01:29:47,518
Your only concern is food, only food.

939
01:29:47,519 --> 01:29:49,639
Who did you get this from?

940
01:29:49,640 --> 01:29:53,799
Really Ghazi, who did you get it from?

941
01:29:54,800 --> 01:29:58,558
Father, you know I got it from you.

942
01:29:59,559 --> 01:30:01,518
True.

943
01:30:04,360 --> 01:30:06,839
You are right.

944
01:30:09,240 --> 01:30:10,719
Ghazi.

945
01:30:10,720 --> 01:30:11,759
I am hungry.

946
01:30:11,760 --> 01:30:14,399
Don't waste time. Come on.

947
01:30:14,400 --> 01:30:17,279
See?

948
01:30:17,280 --> 01:30:19,359
He also turned Yigit to himself.

949
01:30:21,280 --> 01:30:24,119
I feel so thirsty.

950
01:30:24,120 --> 01:30:25,639
Sister, come on, come here.

951
01:30:25,640 --> 01:30:27,079
Give me some water.

952
01:30:34,880 --> 01:30:38,499
Thank you. In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

953
01:30:40,920 --> 01:30:45,558
I am still thirsty. Sister,
come, give me some more.

954
01:30:45,559 --> 01:30:46,598
Alright.

955
01:30:50,760 --> 01:30:53,239
Thank you.

956
01:30:53,240 --> 01:30:55,199
In the name of Allah.

957
01:30:59,640 --> 01:31:03,558
I am still thirsty.

958
01:31:03,559 --> 01:31:05,439
Give me some more.

959
01:31:06,880 --> 01:31:08,079
Thank you.

960
01:31:08,160 --> 01:31:10,039
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

961
01:31:10,080 --> 01:31:13,999
You've become really thirsty, my
Hatun. Did you come here running?

962
01:31:16,240 --> 01:31:18,039
Thanks to Allah.

963
01:31:18,040 --> 01:31:19,679
Thank you sister.

964
01:31:19,680 --> 01:31:20,719
Enjoy.

965
01:31:22,280 --> 01:31:24,759
I'll go and check around.

966
01:31:24,760 --> 01:31:26,399
Sure.

967
01:31:26,400 --> 01:31:27,479
Come on.

968
01:31:27,480 --> 01:31:28,119
Go.

969
01:31:29,720 --> 01:31:31,399
Come on!

970
01:31:31,400 --> 01:31:34,359
Come. I'll show you something.

971
01:31:38,440 --> 01:31:44,518
At the last moment, we had to retreat,
my Emperor, but we were very close.

972
01:31:44,519 --> 01:31:47,719
Being very close does not change anything.

973
01:31:47,720 --> 01:31:49,679
Goynuk is still in their hands.

974
01:31:52,200 --> 01:31:55,119
Also, Mudurnu is still in their hands.

975
01:31:55,120 --> 01:31:58,799
And Lord Nikitas died.

976
01:31:58,800 --> 01:32:01,879
Osman is advancing more day by day.

977
01:32:01,880 --> 01:32:05,359
And you cannot stop him!

978
01:32:05,360 --> 01:32:07,839
Osman entered Mudurnu.

979
01:32:09,200 --> 01:32:11,999
But he will not get out of there alive, sir.

980
01:32:14,120 --> 01:32:17,119
All wells have been poisoned.

981
01:32:18,559 --> 01:32:21,919
Osman will check the water before using it.

982
01:32:21,920 --> 01:32:24,119
Sofia is right.

983
01:32:24,120 --> 01:32:27,558
How are you so sure your plan will work?

984
01:32:27,559 --> 01:32:31,639
The poison does not show itself at first, sir.

985
01:32:31,640 --> 01:32:34,999
It takes time. So they will not suspect anything.

986
01:32:35,000 --> 01:32:40,639
Then it spreads through the
body and gives such pain that...

987
01:32:43,720 --> 01:32:46,558
They will not find an
antidote either. Don't worry.

988
01:32:46,559 --> 01:32:47,558
Good.

989
01:32:48,400 --> 01:32:53,039
I liked that you did not stop fighting
even while retreating, Claudius.

990
01:32:53,040 --> 01:32:59,439
Also, it will be very useful for
the big plan I prepared for Osman.

991
01:32:59,440 --> 01:33:03,079
What do you have in mind, sir?

992
01:33:03,080 --> 01:33:07,839
We will surround Osman from all
sides at his most vulnerable moment...

993
01:33:08,120 --> 01:33:11,598
...and strike a blow that
they have never seen before.

994
01:33:11,920 --> 01:33:12,679
How?

995
01:33:13,280 --> 01:33:17,279
Be patient Claudius.
You will learn after dinner.

996
01:33:22,360 --> 01:33:24,999
Draw water from the well.

997
01:33:25,440 --> 01:33:29,039
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

998
01:33:29,040 --> 01:33:30,359
In the name of Allah.

999
01:33:33,280 --> 01:33:34,279
Allah.

1000
01:33:42,040 --> 01:33:43,439
In the name of Allah.

1001
01:33:50,920 --> 01:33:51,879
My Gonca.

1002
01:33:53,200 --> 01:33:54,558
My Alaeddin.

1003
01:33:54,559 --> 01:33:56,079
Are you alright, my rose?

1004
01:33:56,160 --> 01:33:57,719
I am alright.

1005
01:33:57,720 --> 01:33:59,799
Are you alright, Alaeddin?

1006
01:33:59,800 --> 01:34:02,199
You haven't slept for days.

1007
01:34:02,200 --> 01:34:03,598
You seem tired.

1008
01:34:03,599 --> 01:34:07,999
I am alright, my rose. Don't worry about me.

1009
01:34:08,000 --> 01:34:10,359
We conquered Mudurnu.

1010
01:34:10,360 --> 01:34:12,359
My Halime is alright.

1011
01:34:12,920 --> 01:34:14,759
All my tiredness disappeared.

1012
01:34:14,760 --> 01:34:17,159
Thanks to Allah.

1013
01:34:17,160 --> 01:34:19,279
Would you like to drink some water?

1014
01:34:19,280 --> 01:34:21,679
Drink some water.

1015
01:34:21,800 --> 01:34:24,479
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1016
01:34:26,480 --> 01:34:28,319
Here.

1017
01:34:31,440 --> 01:34:33,119
Hatun..

1018
01:34:34,599 --> 01:34:38,518
I don't want water...
I am really hungry.

1019
01:34:38,519 --> 01:34:39,919
What are we going to do?

1020
01:34:42,120 --> 01:34:44,159
You are hungry?

1021
01:34:44,160 --> 01:34:48,039
Allah Allah, I am really surprised, Alaeddin.

1022
01:34:48,040 --> 01:34:50,919
You are surprised, huh?

1023
01:34:50,920 --> 01:34:53,639
Your husband asks for food,
and you are mocking with him.

1024
01:34:53,640 --> 01:34:56,309
-No way, would I ever do that?
-That's what you are doing.

1025
01:34:56,309 --> 01:34:58,719
No, towbah.

1026
01:34:58,720 --> 01:35:02,159
Good. Come then.

1027
01:35:02,160 --> 01:35:04,319
So you can eat some food, huh?

1028
01:35:04,320 --> 01:35:07,598
You sometimes get hungry then, alright.

1029
01:35:07,599 --> 01:35:08,759
Sometimes.

1030
01:35:08,760 --> 01:35:11,119
Sometimes. You sometimes get hungry.

1031
01:35:18,840 --> 01:35:20,639
Stupid Claudius!

1032
01:35:23,280 --> 01:35:26,239
He thought he could defeat Osman!

1033
01:35:26,240 --> 01:35:33,199
You lost again!

1034
01:36:06,760 --> 01:36:14,399
Your defeat will give me
a new tribe and new lands.

1035
01:36:16,000 --> 01:36:18,879
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1036
01:36:18,880 --> 01:36:20,598
How dare you?!

1037
01:36:20,599 --> 01:36:23,639
The water is poisonous!

1038
01:36:23,640 --> 01:36:26,999
Claudius have poisoned the wells.

1039
01:36:30,400 --> 01:36:33,959
Poisonous, huh?

1040
01:36:35,480 --> 01:36:38,999
But Hasan checked all the waters.

1041
01:36:39,000 --> 01:36:41,558
They said it was safe.

1042
01:36:41,559 --> 01:36:45,399
This poison hides itself until it brings death...

1043
01:36:45,400 --> 01:36:48,679
..and kills immediately.

1044
01:36:48,680 --> 01:36:50,679
Claudius..

1045
01:36:52,400 --> 01:36:55,439
You will take your revenge with this poison, huh?

1046
01:37:14,200 --> 01:37:15,558
Attention!

1047
01:37:15,559 --> 01:37:16,719
Osman Bey!

1048
01:37:22,120 --> 01:37:24,319
Peace be upon you.

1049
01:37:24,320 --> 01:37:27,558
Peace be upon you too, my Bey.

1050
01:37:31,000 --> 01:37:33,319
You may sit.

1051
01:37:33,320 --> 01:37:36,839
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1052
01:37:46,720 --> 01:37:49,598
May our victory be blessed.

1053
01:37:49,599 --> 01:37:55,359
After Goynuk, Mudurnu has
also become the land of Turks.

1054
01:37:55,360 --> 01:37:58,558
We still have a long way to
and many castles to conquer.

1055
01:37:58,720 --> 01:38:01,039
Come on now. Don't let the meals get cold.

1056
01:38:01,040 --> 01:38:01,879
Eat.

1057
01:38:02,599 --> 01:38:05,399
Enjoy.

1058
01:38:05,400 --> 01:38:08,279
In the name of Allah, 
the merciful, the compassionate.

1059
01:38:10,440 --> 01:38:12,999
Here my daughter.

1060
01:38:13,000 --> 01:38:15,479
Here, sister.

1061
01:38:26,800 --> 01:38:28,639
Thank you, brother.

1062
01:38:36,840 --> 01:38:39,039
Sister...

1063
01:38:39,040 --> 01:38:42,518
These meals are not as delicious
as the ones we cooked, right?

1064
01:38:42,519 --> 01:38:44,959
Right, sister.

1065
01:38:44,960 --> 01:38:47,319
Look... This is not how you should cook the meat.

1066
01:38:47,320 --> 01:38:50,279
But you cook meat like a master.

1067
01:38:52,599 --> 01:38:57,799
When my Fatma was afraid of
losing her sister, she forgave her.

1068
01:38:57,800 --> 01:38:59,079
They made peace.

1069
01:39:00,519 --> 01:39:04,399
I knew it, my Bala. I knew this would happen.

1070
01:39:07,200 --> 01:39:10,159
My sister, did you say she'd cook it well?

1071
01:39:10,160 --> 01:39:12,999
No, she cannot cook.

1072
01:39:13,000 --> 01:39:16,159
She just thinks she can cook. Right, my Hatun?

1073
01:39:16,160 --> 01:39:20,839
Brother... -No..

1074
01:39:21,000 --> 01:39:23,919
It was really good
although it was her first time.

1075
01:39:23,920 --> 01:39:29,719
Do you think it is easy to cook, Alaeddin Bey?

1076
01:39:29,720 --> 01:39:33,359
Is that so?
-Right.

1077
01:39:33,360 --> 01:39:35,239
My daughters cook well.

1078
01:39:35,240 --> 01:39:37,679
They do, my Bey. They do.

1079
01:39:38,000 --> 01:39:41,279
In this family, I am always
the one who is left out anyway.

1080
01:39:42,559 --> 01:39:44,159
Do not make my son upset!

1081
01:39:44,160 --> 01:39:46,079
His mother is always behind him!

1082
01:39:46,080 --> 01:39:47,079
My dear mother...

1083
01:39:47,080 --> 01:39:50,039
Good thing I have my mother
with me... Or you would torture me.

1084
01:39:50,040 --> 01:39:51,639
My son.

1085
01:39:51,640 --> 01:39:53,319
Mother.

1086
01:39:53,320 --> 01:39:57,558
Is he acting like this because
my he was born in a cave?

1087
01:39:57,559 --> 01:39:59,719
Fatma.

1088
01:39:59,720 --> 01:40:02,759
Is that what you are saying, Fatma Hatun?

1089
01:40:02,760 --> 01:40:05,199
You'll need my help one day for sure.

1090
01:40:13,800 --> 01:40:20,999
As long as Osman Bey leads the way, none
of those castles can stop us, Hasan Bey.

1091
01:40:21,840 --> 01:40:23,839
Right, Yigit brother?

1092
01:40:23,840 --> 01:40:26,439
Right, brother. True.

1093
01:40:27,580 --> 01:40:30,319
I swear we can conquer all, Koca Bey.

1094
01:40:30,320 --> 01:40:36,199
We first conquered Goynuk after
we left the tribe. And now, Mudurnu.

1095
01:40:36,200 --> 01:40:38,079
May it last, God willing.

1096
01:40:38,080 --> 01:40:40,079
God willing, God willing Hasan Bey.

1097
01:40:40,080 --> 01:40:41,679
God willing

1098
01:40:45,800 --> 01:40:47,518
Enjoy, uncle.

1099
01:40:47,519 --> 01:40:50,279
You seem happy.

1100
01:40:50,280 --> 01:40:54,598
Thank you, my nephew.

1101
01:40:54,599 --> 01:40:56,679
We took Mudurnu.

1102
01:40:56,680 --> 01:40:58,719
We took Goynuk.

1103
01:40:58,720 --> 01:41:01,359
Why would I not be happy?

1104
01:41:08,120 --> 01:41:11,879
We will conquer many lands together.

1105
01:41:16,840 --> 01:41:20,399
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1106
01:41:27,120 --> 01:41:30,558
Drink some sherbet. Ulgen
prepared this sherbet for Halime.

1107
01:41:30,559 --> 01:41:33,999
I asked her to prepare more.
It will take your tiredness away.

1108
01:41:46,720 --> 01:41:49,159
My Ulgen...

1109
01:41:50,120 --> 01:41:54,039
Are you alright, my Hatun? You seem pale.

1110
01:41:54,790 --> 01:41:58,119
I am alright. I am...

1111
01:42:29,680 --> 01:42:31,879
What happened brother?

1112
01:42:31,880 --> 01:42:34,679
May it be good God willing.

1113
01:42:36,720 --> 01:42:39,279
Allah Allah..

1114
01:42:40,000 --> 01:42:42,119
Come on brother. Come on..

1115
01:42:42,120 --> 01:42:45,039
You'll be alright.

1116
01:42:50,840 --> 01:42:52,359
What is happening here?!

1117
01:42:52,360 --> 01:42:55,799
No one understood what it was, Hasan
Bey. Everyone is getting sick one by one.

1118
01:42:55,800 --> 01:42:59,439
The horses and sheep that
drank water in the morning died too.

1119
01:42:59,440 --> 01:43:00,759
The water...

1120
01:43:00,760 --> 01:43:03,679
The water is poisoned.

1121
01:43:08,080 --> 01:43:10,319
Send the Alps to the wells. Come on!

1122
01:43:10,320 --> 01:43:12,439
No one else should drink the water. Go!

1123
01:43:12,440 --> 01:43:14,359
As you order, Hasan Bey.

1124
01:43:14,360 --> 01:43:16,799
My Allah..

1125
01:43:16,800 --> 01:43:19,839
My Allah, help me stay calm.

1126
01:43:19,840 --> 01:43:25,039
Help us, my Allah.

1127
01:43:29,400 --> 01:43:31,119
I am alright..

1128
01:43:31,120 --> 01:43:34,079
My Ulgen, what is happening?

1129
01:43:34,080 --> 01:43:35,719
Mother, you sweat a lot.

1130
01:43:44,480 --> 01:43:46,518
Here we go.

1131
01:43:53,519 --> 01:43:55,719
-Mother.
-What's going on?

1132
01:43:55,840 --> 01:43:57,319
-Mother.
-Alaaddin.

1133
01:43:57,400 --> 01:43:59,479
-Ulgen.
Cerkutay, my stomach...

1134
01:43:59,599 --> 01:44:01,639
-My stomach...
-Ulgen.

1135
01:44:01,840 --> 01:44:02,919
Ulgen.

1136
01:44:02,960 --> 01:44:04,279
What's going on?
-Mother.

1137
01:44:04,280 --> 01:44:06,279
Ulgen, do you hear me?

1138
01:44:06,400 --> 01:44:08,598
She said she has a stomachache.
-Ulgen.

1139
01:44:08,640 --> 01:44:11,159
She turned all pale and
said she had a stomachache.

1140
01:44:11,200 --> 01:44:13,079
My Ulgen? Ulgen?

1141
01:44:13,240 --> 01:44:15,679
-Ulgen, do you hear me?
-Ulgen?

1142
01:44:15,840 --> 01:44:18,399
Hold on, Ulgen.

1143
01:44:22,880 --> 01:44:25,598
Father, something is happening to the alps.

1144
01:44:30,880 --> 01:44:33,518
My Shahzade, do something. My Shahzade...

1145
01:44:35,000 --> 01:44:36,999
They got poisoned.

1146
01:44:41,040 --> 01:44:45,879
-Cerkutay Bey, come on! To the healing house!
-Hold on, my Ulgen. Hold on.

1147
01:44:46,760 --> 01:44:50,558
-Come on.
-Cerkutay. She will be alright, brother.

1148
01:44:50,800 --> 01:44:53,901
Take the poisoned ones
to the healing house quickly!

1149
01:44:53,913 --> 01:44:55,239
Come on, my Shahzade.

1150
01:44:55,840 --> 01:44:58,119
I also feel dizzy, brother.

1151
01:45:00,960 --> 01:45:02,558
Hasan Bey!

1152
01:45:05,040 --> 01:45:06,518
Hasan Bey!

1153
01:45:06,840 --> 01:45:09,799
Nobody drink water! Nobody!

1154
01:45:11,599 --> 01:45:13,799
My Bey, the water is poisoned.

1155
01:45:13,800 --> 01:45:17,518
-The animals that drank water has died.
-Are you saying that just now?

1156
01:45:17,519 --> 01:45:20,799
I examined it but the poisoned took effect later.

1157
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:23,439
-I'm sorry.
-Hasan Bey.

1158
01:45:25,000 --> 01:45:26,518
Alps!

1159
01:45:26,640 --> 01:45:28,839
Clean the wells immediately!

1160
01:45:30,800 --> 01:45:32,439
I can't stand anymore, brother.

1161
01:45:36,200 --> 01:45:39,079
My Bey, you drank water too.

1162
01:45:44,760 --> 01:45:46,879
I'm good. Don't worry.

1163
01:45:53,280 --> 01:45:54,999
My emperor.

1164
01:45:56,280 --> 01:46:00,279
You still didn't tell us what kind
of game you prepared for Osman.

1165
01:46:01,200 --> 01:46:04,439
Be patient, Claudius. You will see soon.

1166
01:46:29,840 --> 01:46:35,079
This is the sign of the divine guardians of Rome.

1167
01:46:38,280 --> 01:46:41,999
-The greatest army of Rome.
-The Guardians.

1168
01:46:43,640 --> 01:46:49,759
Tens of ships carrying blood-thirsty soldiers
are going to reach the land tomorrow morning.

1169
01:46:52,720 --> 01:46:57,999
This army won't kill only Osman...

1170
01:46:59,400 --> 01:47:06,359
...but also everyone in the frontiers
and actually all the Turks in Anatolia.

1171
01:47:07,080 --> 01:47:13,719
I was expecting something big
but I couldn't guess this much.

1172
01:47:14,080 --> 01:47:18,598
The Guardians are coming in
trading ships to hide themselves.

1173
01:47:19,000 --> 01:47:21,479
You two will welcome them.

1174
01:47:21,599 --> 01:47:25,879
Together, we will destroy
whatever belongs to Osman.

1175
01:47:27,040 --> 01:47:30,679
I will wipe out the name of Kayi.

1176
01:47:31,720 --> 01:47:35,079
There won't be a single tent left.

1177
01:47:37,559 --> 01:47:39,639
We will have much fun, huh?

1178
01:47:39,760 --> 01:47:44,639
It will be very enjoyable to
destroy Kayi with this army.

1179
01:47:44,880 --> 01:47:51,999
But before you go there tomorrow, you
need to find out what happened in Mudurnu.

1180
01:47:52,640 --> 01:47:57,279
Your spy will open the gates of
Mudurnu and Goynuk for The Guardians.

1181
01:47:57,400 --> 01:47:59,639
Of course, my emperor.

1182
01:48:00,120 --> 01:48:03,839
Then we should leave without wasting time.

1183
01:48:05,080 --> 01:48:07,119
Excuse me.

1184
01:48:16,640 --> 01:48:20,079
My Ulgen... Ulgen, my wife.

1185
01:48:20,280 --> 01:48:22,598
My Ulgen? Ulgen?

1186
01:48:23,120 --> 01:48:24,999
My Ulgen.

1187
01:48:26,800 --> 01:48:28,239
Gulce.

1188
01:48:28,559 --> 01:48:30,399
Boil basils and thymes.

1189
01:48:30,519 --> 01:48:33,558
Add french lavenders too. It will cure the blood.

1190
01:48:35,160 --> 01:48:38,119
Well... Bring alant too.

1191
01:48:38,160 --> 01:48:41,239
-It strengthens the lungs. Hurry
up -Of course, my Shahzade.

1192
01:48:41,240 --> 01:48:42,558
Come on.

1193
01:48:47,760 --> 01:48:50,799
Hatun, make Ulgen drink this.

1194
01:48:50,920 --> 01:48:52,479
Alright.

1195
01:48:52,920 --> 01:48:54,719
Your cure is here.

1196
01:48:55,400 --> 01:49:00,359
-Come on, Ulgen. In the name of Allah!
-Come on, Ulgen. Drink it.

1197
01:49:00,559 --> 01:49:03,439
O Healer, O Healer, O Healer

1198
01:49:03,559 --> 01:49:06,439
Drink a little more Ulgen. Hold on.

1199
01:49:06,640 --> 01:49:08,399
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1200
01:49:08,480 --> 01:49:11,518
O Healer, O Healer!

1201
01:49:13,480 --> 01:49:15,119
Mother.

1202
01:49:15,320 --> 01:49:16,479
Don't die, mother.

1203
01:49:16,720 --> 01:49:18,879
I promise I will never upset you again.

1204
01:49:19,160 --> 01:49:20,759
I swear, mother.

1205
01:49:20,800 --> 01:49:25,239
Don't say such things, Ghazi.
Your mother will be alright.

1206
01:49:25,440 --> 01:49:29,079
Your mother will be alright.
She'll be alright, my boy.

1207
01:49:29,400 --> 01:49:31,359
Mother...

1208
01:49:32,120 --> 01:49:33,518
Mother.

1209
01:49:35,400 --> 01:49:38,558
She has a high fever, Cerkutay Bey.

1210
01:49:39,640 --> 01:49:41,959
Did Ulgen drink too much water?

1211
01:49:42,040 --> 01:49:45,799
When she came home, she drank half a bottle.

1212
01:49:46,320 --> 01:49:49,279
So... Did she drink during the dinner?

1213
01:49:50,360 --> 01:49:54,439
-It's affecting Ulgen too fast.
-She did, my Shahzade.

1214
01:49:56,720 --> 01:49:59,159
She said she was thirsty and kept drinking.

1215
01:49:59,160 --> 01:50:00,999
Did she?

1216
01:50:05,000 --> 01:50:06,598
Mother.

1217
01:50:16,640 --> 01:50:19,239
-Ghazi.
-Mother.

1218
01:50:21,280 --> 01:50:23,199
Don't cry, my dear.

1219
01:50:26,320 --> 01:50:27,919
Cerkutay.

1220
01:50:28,040 --> 01:50:30,479
Ulgen, my wife.

1221
01:50:30,760 --> 01:50:34,919
It's like my body is melting, Cerkutay.

1222
01:50:35,920 --> 01:50:39,518
My lungs are burning.

1223
01:50:43,040 --> 01:50:44,319
Am I going to die?

1224
01:50:44,480 --> 01:50:46,558
-Cerkutay.
-Mother.

1225
01:50:46,840 --> 01:50:48,119
Am I going to die?

1226
01:50:48,280 --> 01:50:51,879
I won't let that happen. You are strong.

1227
01:50:52,040 --> 01:50:54,518
You can fight this, my Ulgen.

1228
01:50:54,760 --> 01:50:58,119
She can. My mother can.

1229
01:50:58,320 --> 01:51:00,919
Mother? Mother?
-Ulgen?

1230
01:51:00,960 --> 01:51:02,639
-Ulgen?
-Mother?

1231
01:51:03,160 --> 01:51:06,359
-Mother!
-Ulgen! Ulgen

1232
01:51:06,720 --> 01:51:08,199
Mother!

1233
01:51:09,599 --> 01:51:11,558
Don't leave me, mother!

1234
01:51:12,160 --> 01:51:15,239
-How can I live without you?
-My Ulgen?

1235
01:51:15,800 --> 01:51:17,759
Mother.

1236
01:51:19,080 --> 01:51:22,319
-Come here.
-Ulgen.

1237
01:51:23,760 --> 01:51:27,679
-Ghazi. Ghazi.
No! My mother...

1238
01:51:28,040 --> 01:51:32,199
-Come here.
-Mother, don't leave me.

1239
01:51:32,880 --> 01:51:35,679
Come here and pray for your mother.

1240
01:51:35,920 --> 01:51:39,919
-Mother.
-Come on, pray for her.

1241
01:51:40,120 --> 01:51:46,039
Mother, her fever is too high.

1242
01:51:46,360 --> 01:51:48,479
Don't go, my wife.

1243
01:51:48,760 --> 01:51:52,719
Don t leave me. Don't

1244
01:51:53,280 --> 01:51:55,039
Don't.

1245
01:52:10,840 --> 01:52:12,199
My Bey.

1246
01:52:14,040 --> 01:52:19,959
What will I do now?
She will be alright. Don't worry.

1247
01:52:26,480 --> 01:52:28,479
She will be alright.

1248
01:52:28,920 --> 01:52:31,399
Alaaddin, is she alright?

1249
01:52:31,720 --> 01:52:35,639
She drank too much water,
mother. It's affecting her too fast.

1250
01:52:35,800 --> 01:52:37,799
What about the antidote?

1251
01:52:38,840 --> 01:52:40,999
I'm trying to find, mother.

1252
01:52:41,120 --> 01:52:42,839
I'm doing my best.

1253
01:52:45,559 --> 01:52:47,639
Your father drank water too.

1254
01:52:50,200 --> 01:52:52,159
My father?

1255
01:53:08,960 --> 01:53:11,039
I trust you.

1256
01:53:11,960 --> 01:53:14,839
I won't disappoint you, father.

1257
01:53:29,280 --> 01:53:33,119
Innkeeper, bring food to us.

1258
01:53:33,400 --> 01:53:37,439
No food left, stranger. As
you see, we are closing.

1259
01:53:39,599 --> 01:53:42,119
Obviously, they are preparing for something.

1260
01:53:47,240 --> 01:53:49,598
Food here can feed an army.

1261
01:53:50,000 --> 01:53:53,239
It seems soldiers are going to eat here.

1262
01:53:53,400 --> 01:53:57,598
But why would they want to stay here?

1263
01:53:57,680 --> 01:54:00,119
You're right, Turgut Ghazi.

1264
01:54:02,720 --> 01:54:05,479
An army is going to eat here.

1265
01:54:14,920 --> 01:54:22,199
You? Sofia's cringing servant Hristo.

1266
01:54:22,840 --> 01:54:25,719
Let me help you.

1267
01:54:26,160 --> 01:54:30,518
This preparation for the emperor's
hidden army coming from Constantinople.

1268
01:54:30,680 --> 01:54:35,279
If an army were coming from
Constantinople, I would know.

1269
01:54:35,440 --> 01:54:37,719
You can't know, Turgut Ghazi.

1270
01:54:37,800 --> 01:54:41,558
Because they are coming in a trading ship.

1271
01:54:41,800 --> 01:54:43,719
They intend to kill all the Kayis.

1272
01:54:45,920 --> 01:54:48,319
Why would I trust you?

1273
01:54:48,880 --> 01:54:52,479
Claudius poisoned the
wells in the castle of Mudurnu.

1274
01:54:52,760 --> 01:54:55,159
Everybody drinking water there is dying.

1275
01:54:55,200 --> 01:54:58,638
With the army coming, they
will burn down everything.

1276
01:54:59,360 --> 01:55:01,679
Believe me, Turgut Ghazi.

1277
01:55:01,960 --> 01:55:06,598
There is food here enough
for an army, Turgut Ghazi.

1278
01:55:07,040 --> 01:55:13,638
If you are lying to me, I will skin you alive.

1279
01:55:16,760 --> 01:55:20,199
Come on, Solgur Agha. Let's go.

1280
01:55:28,320 --> 01:55:30,558
Do I have permission, my Bey?

1281
01:55:30,840 --> 01:55:33,119
Come in, girl.

1282
01:55:38,320 --> 01:55:40,359
Gonca, how is Ulgen doing?

1283
01:55:41,480 --> 01:55:44,079
The poison affected her too much, father.

1284
01:55:44,480 --> 01:55:46,199
She isn't well.

1285
01:55:49,920 --> 01:55:52,119
Hardly breathing.

1286
01:55:52,639 --> 01:55:55,959
And she has a weak pulse

1287
01:55:57,599 --> 01:56:00,119
Alaaddin thinks she's not doing well.

1288
01:56:01,040 --> 01:56:04,119
But he didn't tell Cerkutay Bey.

1289
01:56:08,880 --> 01:56:11,159
What about the antidote?

1290
01:56:13,200 --> 01:56:16,679
They mixed two different
poisons. He couldn't find it yet.

1291
01:56:16,960 --> 01:56:20,518
He can slow it down but too
many people got poisoned.

1292
01:56:20,720 --> 01:56:23,558
The old can't survive.

1293
01:56:23,720 --> 01:56:26,039
The young still resist.

1294
01:56:33,360 --> 01:56:38,199
What kind of demons are they?

1295
01:56:38,720 --> 01:56:41,159
They're doing this to their own people.

1296
01:56:41,760 --> 01:56:44,119
What kind of demons?

1297
01:56:46,280 --> 01:56:49,319
Father, are you alright?

1298
01:56:50,400 --> 01:56:51,839
What kind of demons?

1299
01:56:51,920 --> 01:56:54,919
-Father?
-Osman! Osman.

1300
01:56:56,599 --> 01:56:59,759
Father, you are sweating

1301
01:57:00,040 --> 01:57:02,359
Did you drink water too?

1302
01:57:03,800 --> 01:57:04,879
-Osman.
-Father.

1303
01:57:04,880 --> 01:57:07,439
-Mother.
-I'm fine. I'm fine.

1304
01:57:08,000 --> 01:57:11,319
-Gonca, go let Alaaddin know! Hurry!
-Alright.

1305
01:57:11,680 --> 01:57:13,199
My Osman..

1306
01:57:16,480 --> 01:57:18,119
Father.

1307
01:57:22,200 --> 01:57:23,879
Osman... -My Bey...

1308
01:58:07,280 --> 01:58:09,279
Cerkutay.

1309
01:58:14,720 --> 01:58:17,518
My Ulgen..

1310
01:58:19,880 --> 01:58:24,079
Our son is entrusted to you.

1311
01:58:24,080 --> 01:58:25,719
Ulgen... Don't say that...

1312
01:58:25,720 --> 01:58:28,239
Protect each other.

1313
01:58:28,240 --> 01:58:31,518
Mother, don't say those things!

1314
01:58:31,519 --> 01:58:33,719
You are not going to die, right?!

1315
01:58:33,720 --> 01:58:38,879
You are not going to die...
You will not leave me alone.

1316
01:58:38,880 --> 01:58:43,119
Don't be upset, my dear boy...

1317
01:58:44,040 --> 01:58:47,598
Don't be upset.

1318
01:58:49,200 --> 01:58:53,119
You will hold on Ulgen. You will hold on!

1319
01:58:54,240 --> 01:58:58,239
Alaeddin.

1320
01:58:58,240 --> 01:59:01,279
My father got sick!

1321
01:59:01,280 --> 01:59:03,638
My Bey.. My Bey...

1322
01:59:10,920 --> 01:59:13,839
Don't be afraid..
Don't be afraid..

1323
01:59:16,120 --> 01:59:18,079
My Hatun..

1324
01:59:18,080 --> 01:59:23,279
You will be alright!

1325
01:59:26,120 --> 01:59:28,919
Ulgen..

1326
01:59:28,920 --> 01:59:29,679
Ulgen...

1327
01:59:31,680 --> 01:59:33,679
My Bala.

1328
01:59:36,080 --> 01:59:38,199
My Bala

1329
01:59:39,960 --> 01:59:43,518
My companion...

1330
01:59:45,080 --> 01:59:46,399
My sister...

1331
01:59:48,120 --> 01:59:51,879
Give me your pardon please.

1332
01:59:54,920 --> 01:59:58,359
You did so many things for me.

1333
01:59:59,320 --> 02:00:03,159
It is all yours, Ulgen.

1334
02:00:05,599 --> 02:00:09,959
But don't say that.

1335
02:00:15,200 --> 02:00:16,919
Cerkutay.

1336
02:00:16,920 --> 02:00:18,079
My Hatun

1337
02:00:21,599 --> 02:00:27,319
If you marry another woman, I will haunt you.

1338
02:00:36,559 --> 02:00:39,638
Don't get lonely...

1339
02:00:45,920 --> 02:00:49,119
Do not starve, my Cerkutay.

1340
02:00:53,880 --> 02:00:55,279
Ulgen!

1341
02:00:55,280 --> 02:00:57,719
Mother! Mother, don't!

1342
02:00:57,720 --> 02:00:59,199
Ulgen!

1343
02:00:59,200 --> 02:01:00,598
I bear witness...

1344
02:01:00,599 --> 02:01:03,679
No! No!

1345
02:01:03,680 --> 02:01:06,799
...and I bear witness that Muhammad is....

1346
02:01:06,800 --> 02:01:08,199
Ulgen...

1347
02:01:08,200 --> 02:01:10,558
...His servant and Messenger.

1348
02:01:10,559 --> 02:01:14,479
Mother! Mother, don't!

1349
02:01:14,480 --> 02:01:16,879
Mother!

1350
02:01:16,880 --> 02:01:19,919
What am I going to do without you?

1351
02:01:19,920 --> 02:01:23,199
Do not leave me, mother!

1352
02:01:23,200 --> 02:01:26,439
What am I going to do here?!

1353
02:01:26,440 --> 02:01:29,959
Why did you leave me alone?!

1354
02:01:29,960 --> 02:01:34,239
Don't die mother! Don't die...

1355
02:01:34,920 --> 02:01:38,839
What am I going to do now, mother?!

1356
02:01:40,280 --> 02:01:44,719
"Indeed we belong to Allah,
and indeed to Him we will return."

1357
02:01:47,080 --> 02:01:50,759
Mother... Mother open your eyes!

1358
02:01:51,559 --> 02:01:53,759
Mother!

1359
02:01:54,559 --> 02:01:59,199
The poison has spread all over Mudurnu.

1360
02:01:59,280 --> 02:02:02,079
They are desperately looking for the antidote.

1361
02:02:02,080 --> 02:02:03,919
Good.

1362
02:02:03,920 --> 02:02:06,598
Let them look for it.

1363
02:02:06,599 --> 02:02:08,279
They won't be able to find it.

1364
02:02:08,440 --> 02:02:13,839
This poison was made from the
snakes and scorpions of Otranto.

1365
02:02:13,840 --> 02:02:18,279
Everyone who believes in Osman will die in pain.

1366
02:02:18,280 --> 02:02:21,479
Including Osman.

1367
02:02:21,480 --> 02:02:24,039
Don't worry.

1368
02:02:24,040 --> 02:02:27,439
Osman is also poisoned.

1369
02:02:27,440 --> 02:02:32,239
He has been barely able
to stand since last night.

1370
02:02:32,240 --> 02:02:35,119
He will soon fall to his deathbed.

1371
02:02:35,120 --> 02:02:36,919
Good.

1372
02:02:37,280 --> 02:02:42,119
I feel sad that he'll die
without seeing Rome's guards.

1373
02:02:42,120 --> 02:02:45,279
I mean... I am almost going to feel sad.

1374
02:02:45,280 --> 02:02:47,719
Rome's guards?

1375
02:02:47,720 --> 02:02:54,079
The emperor's most fierce and
undefeated army is coming here.

1376
02:02:55,920 --> 02:03:02,399
When they arrive, they will burn
everything that belongs to Osman.

1377
02:03:02,400 --> 02:03:04,799
The end of Kayis has come.

1378
02:03:05,920 --> 02:03:07,839
Wait for news from me.

1379
02:03:07,840 --> 02:03:14,079
When we come to Mudurnu
and Goynuk, I will need you.

1380
02:03:14,250 --> 02:03:15,738
Okay.

1381
02:03:25,840 --> 02:03:29,119
It all happened because of me!

1382
02:03:29,120 --> 02:03:31,679
I hurried.

1383
02:03:31,680 --> 02:03:33,679
I acted too quickly.

1384
02:03:36,120 --> 02:03:39,439
I wish you had waited a little longer, Hasan Bey.

1385
02:03:39,440 --> 02:03:42,079
It wouldn't have happened then.

1386
02:03:43,840 --> 02:03:46,159
What is done is done.

1387
02:03:46,160 --> 02:03:50,799
I am afraid of what will happen now.

1388
02:03:50,800 --> 02:03:53,598
Come on Hasan Bey. Come on.

1389
02:03:53,599 --> 02:03:57,719
How would you know the
poison would show itself later?

1390
02:03:57,720 --> 02:04:01,919
Come on!

1391
02:04:02,240 --> 02:04:04,638
Koca Bey.

1392
02:04:04,639 --> 02:04:07,839
What if Alaeddin Bey can't find the antidote?

1393
02:04:07,840 --> 02:04:09,439
My Osman Bey...

1394
02:04:09,440 --> 02:04:11,839
Osman Bey was also poisoned.

1395
02:04:11,840 --> 02:04:18,159
What if something happens to
Osman Bey because of me, Koca Bey...

1396
02:04:20,519 --> 02:04:22,799
Hasan!

1397
02:04:25,400 --> 02:04:28,279
It all happened because of you!

1398
02:04:28,280 --> 02:04:29,959
I didn't know, Cerkutay Bey!

1399
02:04:29,960 --> 02:04:32,638
My Hatun died because of you!

1400
02:04:35,320 --> 02:04:36,959
I couldn't know...

1401
02:04:36,960 --> 02:04:38,039
I did not.. -Shut up!

1402
02:04:38,360 --> 02:04:38,919
Shut up!

1403
02:04:38,960 --> 02:04:40,999
And he is still defending himself!

1404
02:04:41,000 --> 02:04:43,638
People are dying because of you!

1405
02:04:43,639 --> 02:04:45,039
Damn you!

1406
02:04:45,040 --> 02:04:46,919
Cerkutay Bey!

1407
02:04:46,920 --> 02:04:52,279
Do you think I am not suffering in pain, huh?!

1408
02:04:52,280 --> 02:04:54,039
Come!

1409
02:04:54,040 --> 02:04:55,759
Please, don't!

1410
02:04:56,000 --> 02:04:58,079
Stop!

1411
02:04:59,240 --> 02:05:02,439
Stop. Stop, Hasan Bey.

1412
02:05:04,800 --> 02:05:06,479
What are you doing?!

1413
02:05:09,400 --> 02:05:10,839
Pull yourself together!

1414
02:05:12,639 --> 02:05:14,039
What happened to you?

1415
02:05:14,040 --> 02:05:17,999
It all happened because of this careless man!

1416
02:05:18,000 --> 02:05:21,999
Our people and our Osman Bey
have been poisoned because of him!

1417
02:05:24,559 --> 02:05:27,558
He has my Hatun's blood
on his hands, Turgut Ghazi!

1418
02:05:27,559 --> 02:05:30,558
He will pay for this!

1419
02:05:34,240 --> 02:05:35,839
Where is Osman Bey?

1420
02:05:35,840 --> 02:05:37,239
I need to see him now.

1421
02:05:37,240 --> 02:05:39,879
Osman Bey is in his room, Turgut Ghazi.

1422
02:05:48,760 --> 02:05:51,598
Tell me something, my son.

1423
02:05:59,080 --> 02:06:00,919
My father is going to be alright.

1424
02:06:00,920 --> 02:06:05,079
Right, brother?

1425
02:06:07,480 --> 02:06:09,598
The poison spreads.

1426
02:06:12,680 --> 02:06:16,919
There is no way to treat this
illness without finding the antidote.

1427
02:06:35,040 --> 02:06:40,679
You will all die, one by one.

1428
02:06:58,200 --> 02:07:00,759
Look at how majestic they are, Sofia.

1429
02:07:01,000 --> 02:07:07,319
The greatest and undefeated
army of the Roman Empire.

1430
02:07:07,320 --> 02:07:11,598
They will die by the sword of this wild army.

1431
02:07:11,599 --> 02:07:14,638
Osman has also been poisoned.

1432
02:07:14,639 --> 02:07:17,399
He can barely stand.

1433
02:07:17,400 --> 02:07:20,159
The gates are open.

1434
02:07:20,160 --> 02:07:23,638
No one inside is protecting them.

1435
02:07:23,639 --> 02:07:25,479
Look... Do you see?

1436
02:07:25,480 --> 02:07:28,719
Our fate to destroy Osman is written together.

1437
02:07:28,720 --> 02:07:34,719
The sun of Byzantium,
Bitinya will burn the Turks.

1438
02:07:37,320 --> 02:07:38,439
Maybe...

1439
02:07:40,639 --> 02:07:46,439
Maybe that sun will warm your heart a little too.

1440
02:07:52,720 --> 02:07:56,119
You betrayed me.

1441
02:07:56,120 --> 02:08:01,879
Even the fire of hell cannot warm my heart.

1442
02:08:03,680 --> 02:08:09,638
When we kill Osman, my heart
will warm us both. Don't worry.

1443
02:08:13,840 --> 02:08:16,079
To believe this...

1444
02:08:16,559 --> 02:08:23,039
...I need to take it out and
see it with my own eyes.

1445
02:08:32,720 --> 02:08:34,679
Everyone get ready!

1446
02:08:37,000 --> 02:08:44,479
Goynuk and Mudurnu will
become the nightmare of the Turks.

1447
02:08:59,040 --> 02:09:00,999
Father...

1448
02:09:01,000 --> 02:09:02,079
Ghazi..

1449
02:09:02,080 --> 02:09:04,199
Tell me my mother did not die, father.

1450
02:09:06,760 --> 02:09:09,839
Tell me my mother is alive.

1451
02:09:09,840 --> 02:09:14,039
Tell me it was all a dream, father.

1452
02:09:15,440 --> 02:09:16,119
Ghazi..

1453
02:09:19,720 --> 02:09:24,119
Your mother became a martyr.

1454
02:09:30,040 --> 02:09:32,039
Father.

1455
02:09:34,880 --> 02:09:39,399
I am asking you... Is my mother alive?!

1456
02:09:39,400 --> 02:09:41,839
Tell me she is alive, father!

1457
02:09:41,840 --> 02:09:44,638
Tell me my mother is alive, father!

1458
02:09:44,639 --> 02:09:47,159
Tell me my mother is alive!

1459
02:09:52,440 --> 02:09:54,399
Ghazi.

1460
02:09:54,639 --> 02:09:57,518
Ghazi, come here. Come.

1461
02:10:00,080 --> 02:10:02,439
Ghazi, Ghazi.

1462
02:10:02,880 --> 02:10:04,919
Ghazi..

1463
02:10:06,080 --> 02:10:09,999
My mother is dead, Bala Hatun!

1464
02:10:19,240 --> 02:10:22,039
Mothers should never die, Bala Hatun!

1465
02:10:22,200 --> 02:10:24,159
They should never die!

1466
02:10:24,240 --> 02:10:25,959
They shouldn't.

1467
02:10:26,200 --> 02:10:28,759
Mothers never die.

1468
02:10:32,160 --> 02:10:34,799
They always live in the hearts of their children.

1469
02:10:42,599 --> 02:10:45,638
How can I live without my mother, Bala Hatun?

1470
02:10:48,920 --> 02:10:51,959
I know, Ghazi. I know, my dear.

1471
02:10:52,320 --> 02:10:57,719
Yet your mother would never
want you to be upset and cry.

1472
02:10:58,040 --> 02:11:01,959
How can I endure without my mother, Bala Hatun?

1473
02:11:04,200 --> 02:11:07,079
How can I live without my mother?

1474
02:11:14,639 --> 02:11:18,638
Time, my boy... Time, my dear.

1475
02:11:19,800 --> 02:11:22,919
It cures all the wounds.

1476
02:11:28,240 --> 02:11:31,879
A big suffering in your small heart.

1477
02:11:33,519 --> 02:11:37,919
But your mother raised
you as such a strong boy...

1478
02:11:38,720 --> 02:11:40,759
...that you will endure.

1479
02:11:41,720 --> 02:11:46,119
Time will pass and you will grow older.

1480
02:11:46,840 --> 02:11:51,319
And you will be a brave alp.

1481
02:11:52,200 --> 02:11:55,319
You will have many victories.

1482
02:11:55,760 --> 02:12:03,959
Your mother will be happy with your happiness
and wait for you in heaven, my dear.

1483
02:12:54,519 --> 02:12:58,079
Seyit, listen to me carefully.

1484
02:12:59,559 --> 02:13:04,479
You will take over the
watch from Hasan Bey's alps.

1485
02:13:07,480 --> 02:13:10,919
There will be only our alps
on the walls of Mudurnu.

1486
02:13:11,320 --> 02:13:12,999
Come on.

1487
02:13:22,680 --> 02:13:25,879
Well..

1488
02:13:28,440 --> 02:13:31,079
I did my part.

1489
02:13:34,120 --> 02:13:36,879
Now it's your turn, Claudius.

1490
02:14:25,000 --> 02:14:29,759
We'll enter Mudurnu through
the dense forest in the west.

1491
02:14:30,000 --> 02:14:33,799
Osman will never know we are coming, Claudius.

1492
02:14:48,519 --> 02:14:52,959
Undefeated soldiers of Great Rome!

1493
02:14:53,880 --> 02:15:00,399
You take the smell as we
get closer to Mudurnu, right?

1494
02:15:02,240 --> 02:15:09,839
It's the dirty, filthy and
stinking goat smell of Turks!

1495
02:15:13,320 --> 02:15:18,839
While Osman is fighting
against the death in his bed,

1496
02:15:19,040 --> 02:15:23,558
...we will bury them here where they deserve!

1497
02:15:23,840 --> 02:15:25,919
Deep in hell!

1498
02:15:27,160 --> 02:15:29,319
Nobody can stop us!

1499
02:15:29,760 --> 02:15:33,319
-Nobody can stop us!
-Claudius!

1500
02:15:56,440 --> 02:15:58,999
How is that possible?

1501
02:16:05,880 --> 02:16:11,598
As long as I live, I will never let that happen.

1502
02:16:20,720 --> 02:16:22,399
Osman!

1503
02:16:23,120 --> 02:16:29,479
As you didn't die but came to me
yourself, this place will be your grave!

1504
02:16:29,840 --> 02:16:32,679
You won't even have a grave.

1505
02:16:37,000 --> 02:16:42,919
This is a homeland for the
friendly and a grave for the hostile!

1506
02:16:46,760 --> 02:16:52,599
You ruled with blood and will
drown in your own blood now.